    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=972957": {
      "title": "PhD student in Physical Chemistry with focus on perovskite solar cells",
      "description": "PhD student in Physical Chemistry with focus on perovskite solar cells - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student in Physical Chemistry with focus on perovskite solar cells 2026-10-06 The Department of Chemistry - Ångström conducts research and education in the chemistry field. The department has more than 270 employees and has a turnover of 300 million SEK. At the department's six programs, we conduct very successful research of a high international standard. We have a large number of externally funded research projects, often with international cooperation and we see continued good growth in our subject area. The department has education assignments in engineering programs and master's programs. More information is available on our website . www.uu.se/en/department/chemistry-angstrom-laboratory?languageld=1 Duties The research is related to perovskite solar cells (PSCs), a novel photovoltaic technology that has quickly reached efficiencies as high as that of silicon. PSCs are, however, much easier and cheaper to produce. Unfortunately, their stability is still insufficient. Ion conductivity in the material could be the main reason. In this project the PhD student will investigate the ion conductivity in perovskite thin films and solar cells and determine its effect on performance and stability. Furthermore, strategies to control ion conductivity in perovskites will be developed. The PhD student will prepare perovskite films and solar cells in different configurations using wet-chemical deposition methods. Along with vapor-deposited films and solar cell devices from our collaborator, these will be investigated, using electrochemical techniques and advanced spectroscopies. This project is done within the consortium SOLVE - Solar Electricity Research Centre, Sweden (https://www.uu.se/en/research/solve). The main duties of doctoral students are to devote themselves to their research studies, which includes participating in research projects and third cycle courses. The work duties can also include teaching and other departmental duties (no more than 20%). The PhD student should design, plan, perform the experimental work, as well as critically analyze and discuss the results, initially with close guidance by the supervisor. As the PhD students develop, they are expected to become more independent in taking the initiative and planning the research. The students are expected to participate actively in workshops and to present their results at scientific conferences as well as in scientific peer-reviewed journals. Requirements To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must have been awarded a second-cycle degree in chemistry (or a related subject) and possess a good understanding of physical chemistry, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or acquired essentially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. The candidate must have: very good oral and written proficiency in English. Consideration will also be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant’s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. Additional qualifications Previous experience with solar cell research, thin film deposition, electrochemistry and various spectroscopies is desirable. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 1st January 2027 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala, Sweden. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines. For further information about the position, please contact: Gerrit Boschloo, +46 (0)18 471 3303, gerrit.boschloo@kemi.uu.se. Instructions for application The application must contain: A short letter describing your background as well as why you are good match to this position. CV (max. 2 pages) Copy of bachelor exam and transcript of study records Copy of master exam and transcript of study records List of publications including master’s thesis Contact information to at least two references Answer a selection of questions in the application form Please submit your application by 27 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/3013. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Chemistry - Ångström Laboratory Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Fast lönestege Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3013 Last application date: 27 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=974930": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in PET imaging of DPP6",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in PET imaging of DPP6 - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in PET imaging of DPP6 2026-10-06 Are you interested in working with drug development with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favorable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a postdoctoral position at Uppsala University. Department of Medicinal Chemistry at Uppsala University is a strong and international research environment. The department has about 85 employees and here, doctoral students, teachers, researchers and administrators work closely together in a creative and open environment. The position will be based at the Translational PET Imaging research group at Uppsala University and Science for Life Laboratory. The research group focuses on development of molecular imaging methodologies for improved diagnosis, management and treatment of disease. The Translational PET Imaging research group is a part of the Department of Medicinal Chemistry. Project description/Work Duties Type 1 Diabetes (T1D) is associated to the progressive destruction of the beta cells in the pancreas. Emerging treatments include beta cell replacement by transplantation, but novel imaging technologies are needed to monitor the efficacy of such therapies. This postdoc project will develop novel DPP6 targeting PET imaging technologies for monitoring of beta cell mass, with a focus on translation towards early clinical development. The postdoc will receive training in PET radiopharmaceutical development, in vivo molecular imaging technology and regulatory science. The exact description of the tasks depends on the individual skills and research interests of the applicant. The main duties of the applicant are to participate in and lead research projects. The work duties can also include supervision of students, teaching and other departmental duties. Requirements We welcome applications from candidates that have (or soon will have) a PhD degree in pharmacy, biomedicine or related fields, within a maximum of three (3) years before the final application date. During certain circumstances, an earlier PhD can be acceptable. Certain circumstances include leave due to illness, parental leave, work in trade unions, etc. The applicant must have excellent skills in communication and teamwork, and be fluent in English and Swedish. The applicant is expected to work independently and be able to take own initiatives. The assessment of applications is based primarily on the applicant's ability to conduct independent research based on scientific skill. Additional qualifications Previous experience in PET tracer development and/or research in the diabetes field is a merit. Documented courses in radiation protection and/or laboratory animal science are merits. Instructions for Application The application can be written in English or Swedish. In this recruitment, we have replaced the personal cover letter with questions that you answer as part of your application. The answers will be used as part of the selection process. The application should also include a CV, a summary of your previous research experience (max 1 page), and copies of certificates of higher academic degrees and relevant courses (e.g. FELASA or radioprotection).  Please provide a recommendation letter or the contact details (name, e-mail, phone number) for at least one reference such as previous employers or colleagues. Selection process Selection of candidates is based on qualifications, previous experience, and personal suitability. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of two years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date 1 January 2027 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the research project, please contact: Professor Olof Eriksson (olof.eriksson@ilk.uu.se) For further information about the position, please contact: Head of Department Mikael Hedeland (mikael.hedeland@ilk.uu.se) Please submit your application by 30 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2985. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medicinal Chemistry Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2985 Last application date: 30 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=976387": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in gut microbiome epidemiology and cardiometabolic health",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in gut microbiome epidemiology and cardiometabolic health - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in gut microbiome epidemiology and cardiometabolic health 2026-10-06 Are you interested in understanding how perturbations of the gut microbiome may influence cardiovascular and metabolic health? We are looking for a postdoctoral researcher with documented experience in human gut microbiome epidemiology to join the Molecular Epidemiology research group . The position is based in the Molecular Epidemiology research group at the Department of Medical Sciences, Uppsala University. The group investigates the determinants and consequences of variation in the human gut microbiome by combining large population-based cohorts, molecular data and epidemiological methods. The workplace is at EpiHubben, an interdisciplinary research environment bringing together researchers in epidemiology, statistics, genetics, omics and population-based research. The working language is English. The research group is part of the Department of Medical Sciences, a large clinical department with approximately 250 employees and more than 900 affiliated staff through Uppsala University Hospital. The department has a broad research profile, with strong research groups across a wide range of fields. Research is conducted in close connection with clinical activities at Uppsala University Hospital and spans both basic studies of disease mechanisms and the development and evaluation of improved diagnostic methods and new treatments. More information about the department and its activities is available at https://www.uu.se/en/department/medical-sciences/ . The postdoctoral researcher will work on projects investigating the consequences of perturbations of the gut microbiome for cardiovascular and metabolic health. The projects will primarily use large population-based cohorts with gut microbiome data linked to detailed phenotyping, longitudinal exposure information, metabolomics, genetic data and national health registers. Particular emphasis will be placed on longitudinal and causal epidemiological approaches to investigate whether microbiome perturbations contribute to changes in cardiometabolic risk factors and disease. Depending on the applicant’s interest and competence, this may include repeated microbiome measurements, genetic epidemiology and Mendelian randomization. Duties The postdoctoral researcher will take a central role in designing, conducting and publishing epidemiological studies of the gut microbiome and cardiometabolic health. Duties will include: Design of epidemiological studies of gut microbiome perturbations and cardiometabolic health Analysis of large-scale cohort data integrating microbiome, clinical, lifestyle, metabolomic, genetic and register information Apply longitudinal and causal epidemiological methods to strengthen causal interpretation Lead the preparation of scientific manuscripts and presentations Collaborate with epidemiologists, microbiologists, clinicians, geneticists, bioinformaticians and other researchers within national and international collaborations The position is suited to researchers who already have established experience in human gut microbiome epidemiology and who are interested in using longitudinal, molecular and genetically informed approaches to investigate the relationship between the gut microbiome and cardiometabolic health. Requirements A PhD degree in epidemiology, microbiology, medicine or closely related field, where a substantial part of the doctoral research focused on the human gut microbiome in epidemiological studies. The degree must be obtained by the time the employment decision is made. Preference will be given to applicants who obtained their PhD no more than three years prior to the application deadline. The three-year period is calculated from the application deadline. The period may be extended due to special circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave or duties within labour unions. In addition, the applicant must have: Documented research experience in independently analysing gut microbiome data in population-based or clinical human studies Documented research experience related to cardiometabolic health Documented experience integrating microbiome data with phenotypic, clinical, lifestyle or register-based data Strong statistical skills, preferably using R At least one first-author original research article in human gut microbiome epidemiology Excellent written and oral communication skills in English Additional qualifications Experience in one or more of the following areas is considered an advantage: longitudinal or repeated microbiome measurements genetic epidemiology, genome-wide association studies (GWAS) or Mendelian randomization metabolomics or integration of microbiome and other omics data causal epidemiological methods epidemiological studies of antibiotics, medications or other factors that perturb the gut microbiome national health or quality registers About the employment The employment is a temporary postdoctoral position of two years according to the applicable central collective agreement. The position is full time. Starting date according to agreement. Placement: Uppsala. For further information about the position, please contact Professor Tove Fall, tove.fall@medsci.uu.se . Please submit your application by October 21, 2026 , UFV-PA 2026/3007. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medical Sciences Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3007 Last application date: 21 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=937626": {
      "title": "Universitetslektor i onkologi förenad med befattning som specialistläkare vid Akademiska sjukhuset",
      "description": "Universitetslektor i onkologi förenad med befattning som specialistläkare vid Akademiska sjukhuset - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Universitetslektor i onkologi förenad med befattning som ... Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Universitetslektor i onkologi förenad med befattning som specialistläkare vid Akademiska sjukhuset This job advertisement is only available in Swedish . HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=970745": {
      "title": "Researcher in Chemistry",
      "description": "Researcher in Chemistry - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Researcher in Chemistry 2026-10-05 The Department of Chemistry - Ångström conducts research and education in the chemistry field. The department has more than 270 employees and has a turnover of 300 million SEK. At the department's six programs, we conduct very successful research of a high international standard. We have a large number of externally funded research projects, often with international cooperation and we see continued good growth in our subject area. The department has education assignments in engineering programs and master's programs. More information is available on our website. ( https://kemi.uu.se/angstrom/?languageId=1 ). Work duties: The project concerns the preparation of photoactive metal complexes and their application in catalysis of small molecule activation, and has organic chemistry, coordination chemistry and spectroscopy components. The systems will be characterized using traditional organic as well as electrochemical, photochemical and spectroscopic methods. The researcher will develop lanthanide-catalyzed transformations. They will synthesize ligands and their metal complexes, perform chemical and spectroscopic characterization of the complexes, and evaluate their photophysical and photochemical behavior. They will write research reports and publications and present their research results at departmental and group meetings as well as national and international conferences. The position involves the supervision of undergraduate, MSc, and doctoral students, the coordination of laboratory work, and the training of new research group members, and administrative tasks associated with some of these duties. They may also include teaching, up to 20% of the working time. The project will be partly carried out in collaboration with partners at Uppsala University. Am. Chem. Soc. 2023 , 145 , 22555; Org. Lett. 2024 , 26 , 10752; Chem 2025 , 102547; Chem , 2025 , 102450. Requirements : PhD degree in Chemistry or a related subject, or a foreign degree equivalent to a PhD degree in Chemistry. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Post doctoral research experience of at least one year is necessary. The assessment of applications is based primarily on the applicant's ability to conduct independent research based on scientific skill. Greater importance is attached to the quality of individual scientific work, than to the number of publications. Consideration will also be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant’s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. Further requirements: excellent spoken and written English ability to work as a team experience of organic or inorganic synthesis and small-molecule activation experience of photocatalysis, lanthanide chemistry and lanthanide spectroscopy Desirable qualifications: Work experience from the chemical industry, previous experience with supervision of PhD and MSc students, and participation in collaborative research projects is advantageous. About the employment The employment is a permanent position, probationary period may be applied. Scope of employment 100%. Starting date 1 December or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Eszter Borbas, eszter.borbas@kemi.uu.se. Please submit your application by 26 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2780. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Ångström Laboratory Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Permanent position – (starting with a temporary contract) Pay: Individuell Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2780 Last application date: 26 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=975401": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, specialising in data curation",
      "description": "Research Assistant, specialising in data curation - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Research Assistant, specialising in data curation 2026-10-05 Uppsala University, Department of English, The ALMEDA Project African Literary Metadata (ALMEDA) is a research project funded by the European Research Council (ERC) under Horizon Europe, the European Union’s Framework Programme for Research and Innovation (Grant Agreement No. 101097763). The project is based at the Department of English. Duties The duties are associated with the ALMEDA project and primarily include data curation, data entry, and data management in connection with the development of a database. Work hours may also be devoted to annotating source materials. Requirements A university degree at least at the Bachelor’s level in a relevant subject. Good computer skills and experience working with spreadsheet software (such as Excel) or equivalent software. Proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Additional Merits Good knowledge of Linked Open Data and experience working with Wikidata and/or Wikibase is a strong merit for this position An interest in research within literary studies and/or African studies, as well as experience working with cultural or literary source materials. Good familiarity with the field of digital humanities and its methods. Ability to work independently and to work well with others is also given importance About the employment The employment is a temporary position, 6 months. Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date: 1 november or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Ashleigh Harris, ashleigh.harris@engelska.uu.se or Christer Larsson, christer.larsson@engelska.uu.se In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by October 19th, UFV-PA 2026/2969 Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of English Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Special fixed-term employment Pay: Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2969 Last application date: 19 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
