    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=973784": {
      "title": "Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic Chemistry",
      "description": "Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic Chemistry - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic ... Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic Chemistry 2026-09-30 Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic Chemistry The Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences conducts research and education in analytical chemistry, biochemistry, and organic chemistry. More than 100 people, including around 45 PhD students, work at the department. New employees and students are recruited from all over the world and English is the main working language. The department is located at the Biomedical Centre in Uppsala, which facilitates collaborations with research groups in biology, pharmacy, medicine and SciLifeLab and gives access to advanced infrastructure for experimental and theoretical studies. The international environment and good opportunities for interdisciplinary collaborations enables PhD students at the department to participate in relevant research projects and prepare for an international research career. Read more about the research at The Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences at our website . Project description The PhD student will participate in an innovative project involving elements from supramolecular chemistry, molecular recognition, catalysis and chemistry of heavier main-group elements, aiming at discovery of novel routes for selective synthesis. Key analytical techniques to be used include advanced multinuclear NMR as well as other advanced methods for studying molecular structure and molecular interactions. Duties The main duties of PhD students are to devote themselves to their research studies, which includes participating in research projects and third cycle courses. The work duties can also include teaching and other departmental duties (not more than 20 % of full time). Read more about being a Doctoral student here . Requirements To be eligible for doctoral education, a basic higher education equivalent to at least 240 ECTS credits, including at least 60 ECTS credits at Master’s level, including an independent project equivalent to at least 15 credits, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way, is required. More information about the general requirements can be found here . A student has special eligibility for doctoral studies in organic chemistry if s/he has passed courses of at least 90 higher education credits (or equivalent) of courses relevant to the specialization. At least 40 higher education credits must be in organic chemistry at an advanced level (second cycle). More information about the subject specific requirements can be found here . Emphasis will also be placed on personal qualities such as good collaborative skills, motivation, and independence, as well as how the applicant through his/her experience and competence is judged to have the abilities necessary to develop within and acquire the doctoral education. Good English communication, including an ability to clearly disseminate research findings orally and in writing, are essential. Additional qualifications Selection will be based on the applicant’s educational background (BSc as well as MSc level with emphasis on the latter), relevant practical and communication skills and additional experiences relevant for successfully undertaking the PhD education and the project. A background in experimental organic synthesis, the development or investigation of catalytic processes, or the study of non-covalent interactions will be considered favourably. Familiarity with analytical and characterisation techniques such as NMR and UV–Vis spectroscopy, mass spectrometry, X-ray crystallography, and chromatographic methods for purification and analysis would also be advantageous. Relevant experiences, knowledge and skills should be clearly documented in the application and may be exemplified by content and result from taught courses, degree projects, research placements and employments as well as reports, including any publication in international peer-reviewed journals. Doctoral students normally participate for some in teaching at undergraduate and graduate levels. Previous experience from teaching/mentoring, also from environments outside of school/university, as well as other outreach activities may therefore be an advantage. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100%. The intended starting date is 14th January 2027 or as agreed upon. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: (e-mail: andrew.docker@kemi.uu.se) Please submit your application by 29 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2895. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Chemistry - BMC Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Doktorandstege Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2895 Last application date: 29 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=974072": {
      "title": "PhD student position in Bioinformatics/Evolutionary Microbiology",
      "description": "PhD student position in Bioinformatics/Evolutionary Microbiology - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student position in Bioinformatics/Evolutionary Microbiology 2026-09-30 The Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology (IMBIM) at Uppsala University provides a broad international environment for research and teaching. Research at IMBIM spans biochemistry, molecular and cell biology, structural biology, tumour biology, comparative genetics, functional genomics, immunology, bacteriology and virology. The research has a basic-science orientation, with strong relevance to mechanisms of health and disease in both animals and humans. More info: Research – Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology – Uppsala University We are looking for a highly motivated PhD student to join the project “A two-billion-year history of infections: evolution of host-adaptation in early Gammaproteobacteria”, funded by the Swedish Research Council and led by Lionel Guy. The PhD student will be located at the Biomedical Centre, Uppsala, Sweden. Project description The ability to feed on other organisms through phagocytosis is a crucial step in the evolution of eukaryotes, a prerequisite for food webs, multicellularity and probably the acquisition of mitochondria. It also paved the way for intracellular parasitism, as some bacteria avoided digestion by their hosts and multiplied in the nutrient-rich cytoplasm. Here, we focus on the Deep-branching Intracellular Gammaproteobacteria (DIG), a large group of related bacteria (e.g. Legionella and Francisella ) with a wide variety of host-adaptation strategies. We hypothesize that the last common ancestor of DIG appeared during eukaryogenesis, 2 billion years ago, and was among the first bacteria to infect eukaryotes. In this project, the PhD student will gather a solid set of DIG genomes, including isolates belonging to 30 novel species of Legionella , reconstruct their evolutionary history, assess their metabolic potential, and identify their host-adaptation genes. They will screen genomes for horizontal gene transfers from early eukaryotes or Asgard archaea and specifically analyse the evolution of the Legionella genus. A better understanding of the relationships between the first eukaryotes and their early invaders will shed light on eukaryogenesis, and particularly on the role of phagocytosis. Required Qualifications To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in bioinformatics, molecular biology, microbiology, microbial ecology or a similar field or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. The degree should be completed, or expected to be completed, before March 2027. Documented coding skills in Python or R Experience in using and/or developing methods in metagenomics and molecular evolution Background understanding of, and interest in, microbial evolution Proficiency in spoken and written English Ability to plan, carry out and complete research projects independently Creativity and good teamwork skills Desirable qualifications Experience of building pipelines for high-performance computing (HPC) clusters Competence in handling large datasets Experience with DNA extraction and sequencing library preparation The selection is based on the following criteria: completion of the above qualifications, grades in relevant courses, the relevance of those courses to the research programme, and previous experience of work and research in the wider area of the project described above. An overall assessment of the applicant will be made in order to employ the best possible candidate, who can succeed in the doctoral studies and contribute to a positive development of the research programme. Emphasis will be placed on personal qualities, including analytical ability, accuracy, flexibility and collaborative skills. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines . About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date as soon as possible or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further details , please contact Associate Professor Lionel Guy, lionel.guy@imbim.uu.se Application: Please submit your application through the Uppsala University application portal, including a CV, a letter describing your research interests and skills, publications or a copy of your Master’s thesis or equivalent, and contact details for two referees (telephone number and e-mail address). Please submit your application by 29 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2912. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2912 Last application date: 29 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=974523": {
      "title": "PhD student in Media and Communication Studies",
      "description": "PhD student in Media and Communication Studies - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student in Media and Communication Studies 2026-09-30 Are you interested in working with research in Media and Communication, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a position as PhD student in Media and communication studies at Uppsala University. The Department of Informatics and Media has a broad research profile grounded in contemporary research fields, including information systems, interaction design, and media and communication. Within the discipline of Media and Communication Studies , research focuses on various forms of communication and media in both global and local contexts. The work within the research environment is connected through a deeply interdisciplinary and critical approach, employing both qualitative and quantitative methods. We study media and communication as fundamental to understanding contemporary social change as well as to defining the conditions and challenges of human coexistence. Duties The position is a fully funded doctoral studentship in Media and Communication Studies at the Department of Informatics and Media. Doctoral education comprises four years of full-time study. The doctoral candidate is expected to devote the main part of their working time to doctoral education (see project description below) and to actively participate in the department’s seminar activities, workshops, conferences, and similar events. Other duties, such as teaching and research administration – in English and/or Swedish – may also be included as part of the employment (up to a maximum of 20%). The doctoral student will join the project AI Confidential: Emerging Forms of AI Chatbot Use for Emotional Support and Personal Well-being Among Young Swedes , funded by the Swedish Research Council (Grant No. 2026-00497). The project explores how young people (aged 15–18) interpret and relate to AI as a conversational partner in personal areas of life, as well as the opportunities and challenges that traditional healthcare providers experience in relation to this development. The doctoral student is expected to plan and conduct empirical studies within the project, drawing on an existing collaboration with the Youth Guidance Centres in Sweden’s Västmanland Region and working in close collaboration with the research team. The project is led by Matilda Tudor (PI), Media and Communication Studies, and Lina Eklund (co-PI), Human-Computer Interaction; both have research profiles in critical digital media studies and everyday automation. Read more about the project here. Requirements To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in Media and Communication Studies or a closely related/equivalent field, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 90 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, within Media and Communication Studies or a closely related/equivalent field, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. We are looking for a candidate with a strong interest in young people’s living conditions and new technologies. The candidate should have documented experience of working with research-related tasks in Media and Communication Studies, for example through having completed a Master’s-level thesis. The candidate should have documented experience of working with interview methods and/or surveys, and must be able to conduct qualitative research interviews in Swedish. Fluency in Swedish is therefore required, as well as excellent proficiency in spoken and written English. Great importance will be placed on the candidate’s personal suitability for the position and interest in the subject area. In addition to academic qualifications, important qualifications include the ability to collaborate, initiative, independence, and a critical, reflective, and analytical approach. Personal skills should also be substantiated through documentation. When the University appoints new doctoral students, applicants will be selected who, following a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and qualifications, are judged to have the best conditions for carrying out and developing the tasks in question, particularly within the doctoral project, and for contributing to the positive development of activities within the field. Qualifications and merits must be documented in such a way that both their quality and scope can be assessed. Interviews will be conducted either in person or digitally at Uppsala University. Regulations concerning doctoral students are set out in Chapter 5, Sections 1–7 of the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance (Högskoleförordningen), as well as in the University’s rules and guidelines. The application must include: A brief cover letter , which should contain:1) The applicant’s motivation for applying for the position (maximum 500 words). 2) A brief description of the documents submitted (list them). 3) If more than one academic work (thesis, article, etc.) is submitted for assessment, the cover letter must specify which of these the admissions committee should prioritize. Doctoral project plan (maximum two pages, in English). The plan should include the theoretical framework, research questions, aims, type of data, methodology, and timeline. CV with certified copies of academic documents , such as transcripts, demonstrating that the applicant meets the eligibility requirements for doctoral studies in Media and Communication Studies, as well as copies of certified degree certificates and grades. Two letters of recommendation. Copies of independent academic works authored by the applicant as part of their undergraduate or graduate education (C-, D-, or advanced level, or equivalent; drafts of ongoing work may be attached), or other relevant texts. Any other documents the applicant wishes to include. PLEASE NOTE: Incomplete applications will not be considered. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7. Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 1 january or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Project leadar - Matilda Tudor, matilda.tudor@im.uu.se Head of Department – Tomas Eklund, tomas.eklund@im.uu.se Chair of Media and Communication Studies - Michał Krzyżanowski, michal.krzyzanowski@im.uu.se Please submit your application by 13 November 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2934 Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Informatics and Media Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Enligt avtal Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2934 Last application date: 13 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=974531": {
      "title": "Teaching assistant",
      "description": "Teaching assistant  - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Teaching assistant 2026-09-30 Do you want to work on research about the placebo effect, supported by competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Do you want an employer who invests in sustainable employee relationships and offers secure, favorable working conditions? We welcome you, if you are a student at Uppsala University, to apply for a position as an assistant at the Department of Medical Sciences. The Department of Medical Sciences is a large clinical department with around 250 employees and over 900 people affiliated via Uppsala University Hospital. The department has a broad research profile with strong research groups in a variety of areas. Research takes place in close connection to the clinical activities at Uppsala University Hospital and includes both basic studies on the causes of diseases as well as the development and evaluation of improved diagnostics and new treatments. More information about the department's activities can be found at www.medsci.uu.se . Within the research group 'Experimental Cognitive and Affective Neuroscience' (ECAN), led by Associate Professor Malin Gingnell, emotions and cognitive processes are studied from a neurobiological perspective. The work uses experimental psychology in the lab, online, and in combination with various brain imaging techniques (PET, MRI, EEG) to explore behavior and neurobiology in both healthy individuals and in different clinical populations. More information about the group can be found at Experimentell kognitiv och affektiv neurovetenskap (ECAN) – Institutionen för medicinska vetenskaper – Uppsala universitet Duties Job tasks include administration, or participating in research. In a series of research projects, we have explored how the placebo effect develops and affects the treatment of various conditions. In the current project, we focus on an experimental pain model and work with collecting psychophysiology data, EEG data, and using transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) in a lab setting. There are also tasks related to data collection in other projects within the research group. Requirements For employment as a teaching assistant, it is a requirement that you are admitted as a student at undergraduate or advanced level. Personal skills like independence, flexibility, and perseverance, along with the ability to collaborate, are valuable. Good knowledge of English is extremely important, and the role requires a good ability to communicate in Swedish. Additional qualifications For the position, a background in experimental neuroscience, with experience in independently conducting psychological experiments, is considered an asset. Experience with psychophysiological measurement methods, EEG, and TMS is also a plus. Great importance is also placed on other practical research experience, especially if it includes working with participants in a clinical setting. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 12. The position is 40% and work mainly takes place in the afternoons/evenings and on weekends, but mornings can also occur. Start date as soon as possible by agreement and until June 30th 2027. Location: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Malin Gingnell +4670-754 41 48, malin.gingnell@uu.se . Please submit your application by October 14 2026 , UFV-PA 2026 /2933. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medical Sciences Scope: Part-time Working hours: 40% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individual salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2933 Last application date: 14 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=974536": {
      "title": "Research assistant in psychiatry",
      "description": "Research assistant in psychiatry - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Research assistant in psychiatry 2026-09-30 Are you interested in working with mental health research, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a research assistant position at Uppsala University. The Department of Medical Sciences is a large clinical department with around 250 employees and over 900 people affiliated through the Academic Hospital. The department has a broad research profile with strong research groups in a range of areas. The research takes place in close connection to the clinical activities at the Academic Hospital and includes both basic studies on the causes of diseases as well as the development and evaluation of improved diagnostics and new treatment methods. More about the department's activities can be found at medsci.uu.se . Within the research group 'Experimental Cognitive and Affective Neuroscience' (ECAN), led by Associate Professor Malin Gingnell, emotions and cognitive processes are studied from a neurobiological perspective. The work uses experimental psychology in the lab, online, and in combination with various brain imaging techniques (PET, MRI, EEG) to explore behavior and neurobiology in both healthy individuals and in different clinical populations. More information about the group can be found at Experimentell kognitiv och affektiv neurovetenskap (ECAN) – Institutionen för medicinska vetenskaper – Uppsala universitet . Read more about our benefits and what it’s like to work at Uppsala University. Duties As part of the international research project RE-MEND (Building Resilience against Mental illness during Endocrine-sensitive life stages) we study the interaction between the hormonal challenges during puberty and basic psychological functions such as approach behavior, fear extinction, emotion regulation and risk taking. This part of the project focuses on data collection of psychophysiological and fMRI-data. There are also tasks related to data collection in other projects within the research group. Requirements You must Hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in Psychology, Medicine, Biomedicine or any similar field, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. Good knowledge of English is very important, and the position requires a good ability to communicate in Swedish. Additional qualifications For the position, a background in experimental neuroscience, with experience in independently conducting psychological experiments, is an advantage. Experience in using psychophysiological measurement methods and fMRI, as well as experience working with the patient group, is also a plus. Great emphasis is also placed on other practical research experience, especially if it involves working with participants in a clinical setting. Personal skills such as independence, flexibility, and perseverance, along with the ability to collaborate, are valuable. About the employment The employment is a temporary position for 6 months. Scope of employment 40 %. Starting date as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Malin Gingnell +4670-754 41 48, malin.gingnell@uu.se Please submit your application by XX month 2026 , UFV-PA 2026 /2935. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medical Sciences Scope: Part-time Working hours: 40% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individual salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2935 Last application date: 14 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
