    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=974559": {
      "title": "Research assistant in psychiatry",
      "description": "Research assistant in psychiatry - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Research assistant in psychiatry 2026-09-30 Are you interested in working with placebo research, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a research assistant position at Uppsala University. The Department of Medical Sciences is a large clinical department with around 250 employees and over 900 people affiliated through the Academic Hospital. The department has a broad research profile with strong research groups in a range of areas. The research takes place in close connection to the clinical activities at the Academic Hospital and includes both basic studies on the causes of diseases as well as the development and evaluation of improved diagnostics and new treatment methods. More about the department's activities can be found at www.medsci.uu.se. Within the research group 'Experimental Cognitive and Affective Neuroscience' (ECAN), led by Associate Professor Malin Gingnell, emotions and cognitive processes are studied from a neurobiological perspective. The work uses experimental psychology in the lab, online, and in combination with various brain imaging techniques (PET, MRI, EEG) to explore behavior and neurobiology in both healthy individuals and in different clinical populations. More information about the group can be found at Experimentell kognitiv och affektiv neurovetenskap (ECAN) – Institutionen för medicinska vetenskaper – Uppsala universitet Read more about our benefits and what it’s like to work at Uppsala University. Duties In a series of research projects, we have explored how the placebo effect develops and affects the treatment of various conditions. In the current project, we are focusing on an experimental pain model and working on collecting psychophysiology data, EEG data, and using transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) in a lab setting. There are also tasks related to data collection in other projects within the research group. Requirements A completed or ongoing university education in psychology, medicine, biomedicine, or a related field is required for this position. Applicants must have completed at least 180 higher education credits (ECTS), or have otherwise acquired knowledge and skills that are deemed equivalent. Good knowledge of English is of utmost importance and fluency in Swedish is mandatory. Additional qualifications For the position, a background in experimental neuroscience, with experience in independently conducting psychological experiments, is considered an asset. Experience with psychophysiological measurement methods, EEG, and TMS is also valued. Great importance is also placed on other practical research experience, especially if this includes working with human participants in a clinical setting. Personal qualities such as independence, flexibility, and perseverance, along with the ability to collaborate, are valuable. About the employment The employment is a temporary position for 7 months. Scope of employment 40 % with working hours primarily scheduled during afternoons, evenings, and weekends. Some morning work may also be required. Starting date as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Malin Gingnell +4670-754 41 48, malin.gingnell@uu.se . Please submit your application by October 14, 2026 , UFV-PA 2026 /2637. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medical Sciences Scope: Part-time Working hours: 40% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individual salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2937 Last application date: 14 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
