    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=971008": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Offshore Renewable Energy with Specialisation in Computational Methods",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Offshore Renewable Energy with Specialisation in Computational Methods  - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Assistant Professor in Offshore Renewable Energy with Specialisation in Computational Methods 2026-09-29 Do you want to be part of a leading research environment in renewable energy and advance your research at Sweden's largest Faculty of Science and Technology? We are now recruiting an Assistant Professor who will contribute to the development of research and education in offshore renewable energy. The Department of Electrical Engineering conducts multidisciplinary research across the full spectrum of electrical engineering, from technologies for renewable electricity generation and the electrification of the transport sector to 5G/6G communications and smart electrical sensors. The successful candidate will join the Division of Electricity, an international and interdisciplinary research environment with strong expertise in computational science, energy systems, fluid mechanics, and the sustainable energy transition. Research is carried out in close collaboration with national and international universities, research institutes, and industrial partners. The division provides access to advanced high-performance computing infrastructure as well as experimental and numerical facilities supporting research on next-generation offshore energy systems. More information about the Department of Electrical Engineering is available at: https://www.uu.se/en/department/electrical-engineering Subject Area We seek an outstanding early-career researcher who wishes to develop research and education in advanced numerical methods for modelling and simulation of complex physical processes associated with offshore energy systems. The successful candidate is expected to establish an independent and internationally competitive research programme focusing on numerical modelling of fluid–structure interaction and the development of computational tools for next-generation renewable energy technologies. The research should contribute to robust, efficient, and sustainable solutions for floating offshore wind, wave energy, and other marine renewable energy systems. Duties You will work with: Conduct research of the highest international quality. This includes developing and leading an independent research group, collaborating with researchers within the department as well as with international research groups and industry, and contributing to the strategic development of the department and the university. The position also includes actively seeking and securing external research funding. Teaching. Teaching responsibilities include course coordination, course administration, and supervision of undergraduate, master's and PhD students. The successful candidate is also expected to contribute to the development of courses in renewable energy engineering. Participate in departmental administration and contribute to the general academic responsibilities of the Department of Electrical Engineering. This includes serving on committees, taking on responsibilities beyond one's own research and teaching, participating in the evaluation and development of educational and research activities, collaborating with colleagues, and contributing to a constructive academic environment. Maintain up-to-date expertise within the subject area and follow developments in society that are relevant to the position at Uppsala University. Among qualified applicants, selection will be based primarily on scientific and pedagogical excellence, with particular emphasis placed on scientific merits. The ability to secure external research funding, collaborate effectively with external stakeholders, and demonstrate leadership potential will also be considered. Qualifications required You must have: A PhD in a field relevant to the position, such as engineering mechanics, energy systems, fluid mechanics, or a related discipline. Priority will be given to applicants who obtained their doctoral degree, or achieved equivalent competence, no more than seven years before the closing date for applications. Demonstrated scientific excellence in offshore renewable energy, including research relevant to wave energy, floating offshore wind, and related marine renewable energy technologies. Applicants should have documented expertise in one or more of the following areas: fluid mechanics, numerical methods, high-performance computing, optimisation, and the design of complex energy systems. Scientific excellence must be demonstrated through publications in leading international peer-reviewed journals. Demonstrated teaching expertise, with particular emphasis on experience in theoretical, numerical, and experimental education. The ability to integrate research, subject-specific pedagogy, and higher education pedagogy into teaching is considered essential. Completed higher education teaching training equivalent to at least five weeks, or possess equivalent documented competence. If special circumstances apply, such training may be completed during the first two years of employment. Documented ability to teach in Swedish or English. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively and otherwise meet the personal suitability requirements necessary to perform the duties of the position. A documented ability to obtain external research funding in competitive calls. Particular merit will be given to prestigious national or European research grants. Scientific and pedagogical expertise relevant to the subject area and duties of the position. Other desirable/valuable qualifications It would be an advantage if you have: Experience in the development and application of scientific software or numerical methods for offshore renewable energy systems, including physics-based modelling as well as emerging data-driven and AI-enabled approaches. Experience in high-performance scientific computing of offshore renewable energy systems, including advanced CFD-simulations. Experience of industrial research collaborations relevant to the position. International research collaborations and a strong international research network. For more information on assessment and assessment criteria, see the Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University and the Faculty of Science and Technology’s Guidelines for the Appointement and Promotion of Teachers . All qualifications must be documented in a manner that makes it possible to assess both their quality and their scope. When the University appoints new academic staff, candidates will be selected based on a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and expertise, taking into account their potential to perform and develop the duties of the position and to contribute to the positive development of the department. Application Parental leave, part-time work due to childcare, trade union responsibilities, military service or similar activities are treated as work experience and should be listed in the CV. Instructions for applications for employment Period of employment The position of Assistant Professor is fixed-term for up to six years and is intended to provide qualifications for a permanent teaching position with higher eligibility requirements. During the appointment, there is the possibility to apply for promotion to Associate Professor. If the requirements are met and suitability is confirmed, the appointee may be promoted to a permanent position as Associate Professor. About the position This is a temporary full-time position six years. The position is full-time (100%). Starting date 1 March or as agreed. Place of work: Uppsala, Sweden Further information about the position is available from: Karin Thomas, 018-471 3098, karin.thomas@uu.se We look forward to receiving your application by 12 November, UFV-PA 2026/2787 In the event of any disagreement between the English and the Swedish versions of this announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. We offer you Sweden offers good working conditions, including comprehensive social benefits such as generous family-focused policies that make healthcare, childcare, and children’s education available and highly affordable. At Uppsala University, we offer the opportunity for new international staff to learn Swedish through our language courses. If you have family, they will get new contacts and support through the Uppsala International Citizen hub . If you are an international candidate, you will find a lot of information about working and living in Sweden at http://www.uu.se/joinus . Uppsala University’s tenure track system grants assistant professors the possibility to be assessed for promotion to the position as associate professor. The university provides support in various areas, such as scientific and educational development, leadership development as well as patent and innovation support. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Technology, Department of Electrical Engineering Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individually negotiated salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2787 Last application date: 12 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=971429": {
      "title": "Forskningsassistent: Transkribering av Meänkieli",
      "description": "Forskningsassistent: Transkribering av Meänkieli - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Forskningsassistent: Transkribering av Meänkieli Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Forskningsassistent: Transkribering av Meänkieli This job advertisement is only available in Swedish . HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
