    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=970031": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Materials Theory",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Materials Theory - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral Researcher in Materials Theory 2026-09-21 Are you interested in working with materials theory, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employment and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a postdoc position at Uppsala University. Uppsala University is a comprehensive research-intensive university with a strong international standing. Our mission is to pursue top-quality research and education and to interact constructively with society. Our most important assets are all the individuals whose curiosity and dedication make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Uppsala University has 42,000 students, 7,000 employees and a turnover of SEK 6.7 billion. Uppsala University invites applications for a postdoctoral position in materials theory. The Division of materials theory offers world-class research in solid-state theory, using both numerical and analytical methods. The research is focused on magnetism, electronic structures, topological phases, correlation phenomena, and materials for green energy. Duties The postdoctoral position involves working in a larger theoretical research environment focused on the development and application of methods for simulating magnetism, particularly atomistic and multiscale simulations. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to collaborate with leading experimental and theoretical groups at Uppsala University and other Swedish universities with a research focus on functional magnetic materials. Requirements PhD degree in physics or a foreign degree equivalent to a PhD degree in physics. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Priority will be given to applicants who have completed their degree no more than three years before the deadline for applications. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. The successful applicant is expected to have expertise in atomistic or micromagnetic simulation methods. Experience in both software development and the application of these methods is important and will be taken into account in the assessment of applicants. Good communication skills in both spoken and written English. Additional qualifications Experience with development of atomistic- or multiscale simulation methods, e.g in a GPU architecture, and their applications to magnetic phenomena is meriting. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of two years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date December 1, 2026 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala. For further information about the position, please contact: Olle Eriksson +46(0) 704250777 olle.eriksson@physics.uu.se. In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by October 26, 2026, UFV-PA UFV-PA 2026/2752. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Physics, Department of Physics and Astronomy Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Fixed Salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2752 Last application date: 26 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=967690": {
      "title": "PhD student in electrical engineering with focus on power system adequacy",
      "description": "PhD student in electrical engineering with focus on power system adequacy - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student in electrical engineering with focus on power system adequacy 2026-09-18 Electrification and digitalisation are among the major areas for the future transition to sustainable societies. The Department of Electrical Engineering conducts successful research and education in these areas - including renewable energy sources, electric vehicles, industrial IoT, 6G communication, and wireless sensor networks, as well as research and education in Life Science, health technology, smart electronic sensors, and medical systems. The Department of Electrical Engineering is an international environment with around 160 employees who contribute to important technological energy and health at the Ångström Laboratory. We are now looking for a PhD student in electrical engineering with focus on power system adequacy. Come and join us! The position is placed at the Division of Electricity within the Department of Electrical Engineering. Here you will find a welcoming working environment with an active doctoral student network and a variety of experimental projects. The division collaborates with Swedish companies – both public and private – as well as other stakeholders within the various research areas. We look forward to receiving your application. Join us in building the future! Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University Project description Large dependencies of reliable power production from offshore renewable energy systems (RES) is expected in the next decades, in particular onshore and offshore wind and solar PV. Large changes are also seen in energy and electricity supply from non-renewable sources, due to, e.g., recent national policy changes around nuclear power or imported gas and oil. The demand side is transforming as well, driven by changes such as the electrification of transportation and other sectors, and increased use of heat pumps or air conditioning. Finally, climate change is implying changes in weather, with heat waves and other weather extremes affecting society and the energy system. There are large knowledge gaps regarding the power production reliability under severe weather conditions and transforming energy systems. In this project, the student will investigate the security of electricity supply in the European power system in current and future projected scenarios considering transformations in the energy production, energy consumption, and climate. The project is part of the Centre for Natural Disaster Science (CNDS), a national research centre that aims to prevent and improve society's preparedness for risks by increasing knowledge of the dynamics and consequences of natural disasters. Cooperation and communication within the CNDS network provide an interdisciplinary platform for exchanging expertise in natural disasters and risk reduction. The research group at Uppsala University has extensive experience of research in electrical engineering and has a large laboratory activity. We offer a varied and exciting work, planned by the doctoral student and the research group together. The doctoral student will be supervised by at least two supervisors. Duties The main task for a doctoral student is to devote themselves to their doctoral education, which includes both participation in research projects and doctoral education courses. Teaching and other departmental duties may be part of the position, to a maximum of 20% of the working hours. Qualifications required To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in electrical engineering, energy systems engineering, engineering physics or similar, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. Specify other skills, competencies, and qualities that are required for the position. We place great emphasis on personal qualities such as strong motivation, good collaboration and communication skills with other researchers. You should be purposeful, structured and be able to work effectively both individually and in groups. The candidate must have excellent communication skills in English and/or Swedish, both orally and in writing. Qualifications desired Good oral and written proficiencies in Swedish is a merit. Experience in numerical modelling and programming as well as experimental work is a merit Experience from industry is a merit About the employment Fixed term position 48 months, in accordance with Chapter 5, Section 7 of the Higher Education Ordinance. Full-time. Start date as agreed. Location: Uppsala. Rules governing doctoral students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance Chapter 5, Sections 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines . For further information about the position, please contact Head of division, Karin Thomas, karin.thomas@uu.se Professor, Malin Göteman, malin.goteman@uu.se. Application instructions The application should include 1) a cover letter describing yourself, your research interests and why you wish to pursue doctoral studies, 2) your CV, 3) a brief description of your education, 4) a copy of your Master’s degree certificate and course transcripts, as well as a copy of your Master’s thesis, 5) any other documents you wish to refer to, 6) the names and contact details of referees (email address and telephone number), and 7) any publications. You are welcome to submit your application no later than 2 November 2026 . UFV-PA 2026/2671. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Electrical Engineering Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Lönestege Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2671 Last application date: 2 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=967945": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Engineering Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Engineering Sciences - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Assistant Professor in Engineering Sciences 2026-09-18 Are you ready to shape the future of research and education? At Uppsala University, your ideas matter. We welcome top talents in Science and Technology to a world-class environment driving innovation and collaboration. Advance the frontiers of science. It starts with you. The technical section consists of three departments with a total of twelve research programs. We offer a unique interdisciplinary research environment, specialized and well-functioning infrastructures, competitive funding, and good conditions for establishing a new research group. The host institution also offers a start-up package that guarantees your own salary for a five-year period, the salary of a doctoral student or postdoctoral fellow, and resources to establish the research group. The Department of Materials Science and Engineering develops technical solutions in sustainability and energy and educates in our interdisciplinary subject. With the help of innovative researchers and state-of-the-art facilities, we meet today's and tomorrow's challenges in materials science. AI for materials science is an emerging research field that uses machine learning, data analysis and computational modelling to guide the discovery, characterization and optimization of new materials. By accelerating innovation cycles, AI in materials science plays a central role in the development of new sustainable technologies for the society of the future. You can find more information about us here . The Department of Civil and Industrial Engineering conducts interdisciplinary engineering research on infrastructural and industrial socio-technical systems and processes. Our research is strongly linked to sustainable development and is based on extensive interaction with society and industry. The department’s research is conducted within two research programs: Industrial Engineering and Management and Civil Engineering and Built Environment. You can find more information about us here . The Department of Electrical Engineering conducts leading research and education in electrification, digitalization, and health technology, with applications ranging from renewable energy, electrified transportation systems, robotics, AI, and 5G/6G communication to smart sensors and medical technology. In collaboration with stakeholders, we develop medical and electrical systems spanning from materials and manufacturing understanding to the software required. The department is organized into four divisions: Electricity, Integrated Smart Systems Technology, Solid-State Electronics, and Signals and Systems. Together, we create a dynamic and international environment where research and education meet, and where we contribute to technological solutions that shape the future of society—both locally and globally. You can find more information about us here. Your department placement will be determined in connection with the appointment. You will indicate one or more preferred departments as part of the application process. Subject area We welcome you who are researching and teaching in any of the following subject areas: Electrical engineering with a focus on electrification, digitalization or health technology, with applications ranging from renewable energy, electrified transport systems, robotics, AI, 5G/6G communications, smart sensors, or medical technology. The interface between machine learning and experimental materials science. Development and application of machine learning methods in experimental workflows, data-driven experimental design, hypothesis generation or process modeling, deep learning for spectroscopic data or image processing, and applications of physics-informed machine learning. You would also like to have experience in automating data generation chains, for example through the development and application of relevant software and hardware for experiment control and database management. Sustainability Transitions. You have a strong theoretical profile combined with qualitative or quantitative empirical research, for example in our strength areas of life science, energy systems, built environment, and ICT. Organisation and Management with a focus on Artificial Intelligence. You have an established position at the intersection of organization and management studies, sociotechnical change, and AI, and combine theoretical perspectives that problematize core assumptions with empirical research on AI, in particular ethical AI in practice. Urban Infrastructure and Spatial Planning. You have a background in civil engineering with expertise in urban-level spatial analysis of infrastructure systems, addressing challenges such as climate adaptation and infrastructure resilience, sustainable land and resource use, or development of nature-based solutions on the urban scale. Duties You will work with: research. To establish and lead your own research group; publishing research results in internationally recognized peer-reviewed journals and presenting them at leading international conferences; actively applying for and securing external grants. teaching. Teaching includes course responsibility, course administration and supervision of doctoral students. administration. To participate in the general academic duties of the department. This includes serving on committees, taking on responsibilities beyond your own research and teaching assignment, contributing to the evaluation and development of teaching and research activities, working collaboratively with colleagues, and providing support and constructive feedback to colleagues. keeping up to date in your subject area and following developments in society that are relevant to your work at Uppsala University. In choosing between eligible candidates, emphasis will primarily be given to both research and teaching expertise, according particular weight to research expertise. In addition, attention will be given to administrative, management and collaboration expertise Qualifications required You must have: a PhD that is of relevance to at least one of the specified subject areas . Preference will be given to applicants who have completed their PhD or attained equivalent expertise no more than seven years before the deadline for applications. Research expertise within at least one of the specified subject areas. had your main employment and conducted your research activities outside Sweden for at least the past four years immediately prior to the application deadline. Shorter stays in Sweden of a total of no more than twelve months may be accepted. teaching expertise within at least one of the specified subject areas. Ability to link research to teaching, based on the subject concerned, subject didactics and teaching and learning in higher education. completed at least five weeks of teacher training for higher education of relevance to the organization and its activities or be considered to have acquired the equivalent knowledge. The required training for teachers in higher education may be completed during the first two years of employment if there are special circumstances. a documented ability to teach in Swedish or English. ability to work with other people and otherwise meet the demands of suitability required to perform the duties well. documented skills and expertise in productive research collaborations and in successfully leading projects. documented ability to successfully compete for and secure external research funding. teaching expertise and research expertise that are relevant to the subject area and the duties that the position involves. Other desirable/valuable qualifications It would be an advantage if you have: collaboration expertise. Interacting with the wider community, disseminating and exchanging information and translating research and development results into practical benefits. administrative expertise. Capacity to plan, organize and prioritize activities and to work in a structured manner that demonstrates an awareness of goals and quality. management expertise. Developing, coordinating and leading operations and staff. For more information on assessment and assessment criteria, see the Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University and the Faculty of Science and Technology’s Guidelines for the Appointment and Promotion of Teachers . All qualifications must be documented in a manner that makes it possible to assess both their quality and their scope. When the University appoints new academic staff, candidates will be selected based on a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and expertise, considering their potential to perform and develop the duties of the position and to contribute to the positive development of the department. Application Parental leave, part-time work due to childcare, trade union responsibilities, military service or similar activities are treated as work experience and should be listed in the CV. Instructions for applications for employment Period of employment The position of Assistant Professor is fixed-term for up to six years and is intended to provide qualifications for a permanent teaching position with higher eligibility requirements. During the appointment, there is the possibility to apply for promotion to Associate Professor. If the requirements are met and suitability is confirmed, the appointee may be promoted to a permanent position as Associate Professor. About the position Fixed-term employment for a maximum of 6 years. The scope is full-time. Starting date: As agreed (as soon as possible). Location: Uppsala Further information about the position please contact: Professor Klas Hjort, +46 (0)70 425 0597, klas.hjort@angstrom.uu.se We look forward to receiving your application by October 15 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2678. In the event of any disagreement between the English and the Swedish versions of this announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. We offer you Sweden offers good working conditions, including comprehensive social benefits such as generous family-focused policies that make healthcare, childcare, and children’s education available and highly affordable. At Uppsala University, we offer the opportunity for new international staff to learn Swedish through our language courses. If you have family, they will get new contacts and support through the Uppsala International Citizen hub . If you are an international candidate, you will find a lot of information about working and living in Sweden at http://www.uu.se/joinus . Uppsala University’s tenure track system grants assistant professors the possibility to be assessed for promotion to the position as associate professor. The university provides support in various areas, such as scientific and educational development, leadership development as well as patent and innovation support. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individually negotiated salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2678 Last application date: 15 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=970562": {
      "title": "Research Infrastructure Specialist in Cryo-Electron Tomography (Cryo-ET)",
      "description": "Research Infrastructure Specialist in Cryo-Electron Tomography (Cryo-ET) - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Research Infrastructure Specialist in Cryo-Electron Tomography (Cryo-ET) 2026-09-18 Are you interested in developing and applying state-of-the-art cryo-electron tomography (cryo-ET) in a dynamic and interdisciplinary research environment? Would you like to play a central role in establishing the new LINNAEUS laboratory for cryo-ET and enabling cutting-edge research across Uppsala University? We welcome you to apply for a position as Research Infrastructure Specialist in Cryo-ET at Uppsala University. The Department of Cell and Molecular Biology is organized into seven research programmes which all focus on different areas of cell and molecular biology: Computational Biology and Bioinformatics, Microbiology and Immunology, Molecular Biology, Molecular Biophysics, Molecular Evolution, Molecular Systems Biology and Structural Biology. The scientific basis of what we do lies in biology, but our research overlaps with other areas such as medicine, computer science, mathematics, chemistry, engineering sciences and physics. In total, we are over 200 staff and ~60 Ph.D. students. Please read more about the department’s work at https://www.uu.se/en/department/cell-and-molecular-biology . The position will be associated with the Uppsala University's Cryo-EM facility ( https://www.uu.se/en/department/cell-and-molecular-biology/research/infrastructures/cryo-em ), which is an independent cross-program Departmental facility co-directed by Dr. Sundborger-Lunna and Dr. Marcia and open to all scientists at Uppsala University and beyond. The position will contribute to the development of cryo-ET at Uppsala University and facilitate its application across a broad range of research projects, supporting among other activities the newly established Centers for Molecular Dynamics and for Infection Biology, two interdisciplinary initiatives bringing together expertise and infrastructure for studying the structure, dynamics and function of biological systems and mechanisms of antimicrobial drug resistance, respectively. The successful candidate will work closely with researchers from different scientific disciplines, providing expertise in cryo-ET while contributing to the continued development of methods, workflows and infrastructure. The position provides substantial opportunities to participate in collaborative research, develop new cryo-ET approaches and, depending on the candidate's interests and expertise, pursue independent research and method development. Duties The primary responsibility of the position is to facilitate and develop cryo-ET research at Uppsala University and within the Center for Molecular Dynamics. The duties include: Supporting researchers in the design and execution of cryo-ET experiments, from experimental planning and sample preparation to data collection, processing and interpretation. Developing, implementing and optimizing workflows for cryo-ET sample preparation, data acquisition and data processing. Supporting and training users in cryo-ET methods and associated instrumentation and software. Contributing to the establishment, operation and continued development of cryo-ET infrastructure and associated workflows at Uppsala University. Working collaboratively with researchers across different disciplines to identify how cryo-ET can best address their scientific questions. Contributing to method development in areas relevant to cryo-ET and structural and cellular biology. Establishing and maintaining documentation, protocols and best practices to ensure robust and reproducible workflows. Participating in collaborative research projects and, where appropriate, contributing to scientific publications. Opportunities exist to pursue independent research and methodological development within the broader scientific goals of the facility. Requirements The applicant must have: A PhD in structural biology, molecular or cell biology, biophysics, biochemistry, or another relevant field. Hands-on experience with cryo-ET (including sample preparation, data collection and data processing). A strong interest in developing and applying cryo-ET methods to biological research questions. Ability to work independently and take responsibility for developing and maintaining experimental and computational workflows. Excellent ability to collaborate with researchers from different scientific backgrounds. Good communication skills and the ability to explain complex methods and concepts to users with different levels of experience. Excellent command of spoken and written English. Because the position involves extensive interaction with researchers and facility users, particular emphasis will be placed on scientific curiosity, problem-solving ability, service-mindedness, initiative and the ability to work collaboratively in an interdisciplinary environment. Additional qualifications The following experience is considered particularly advantageous: Experience with cryo-correlative light and electron microscopy (cryo-CLEM). Experience with subtomogram averaging and/or advanced cryo-ET image-processing workflows. Experience with commonly used cryo-ET software and computational workflows. Experience developing or implementing new cryo-EM/cryo-ET methods. Experience working in a research infrastructure, core facility or other collaborative research environment. Experience training and supporting researchers in advanced microscopy techniques. About the employment The employment is a permanent position (probationary period may be applied). Scope of employment: 100%. Starting date as agreed. Placement: Uppsala. For further information about the position, please contact : Anna Sundborger-Lunna, anna-sundborger-lunna@icm.uu.se or Marco Marcia, marco.marcia@icm.uu.se . In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as part of the selection process. Please submit your application by 19 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2769. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Cell and Molecular Biology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Permanent position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2769 Last application date: 19 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=970912": {
      "title": "Associate Senior Lecturer (SciLifeLab Fellow) in Antimicrobial Resistance",
      "description": "Associate Senior Lecturer (SciLifeLab Fellow) in Antimicrobial Resistance - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Associate Senior Lecturer (SciLifeLab Fellow) in Antimicrobial Resistance 2026-09-18 SciLifeLab ( www.scilifelab.se ) is a national centre for large-scale, data-driven and hypothesis-driven research in molecular biosciences. Science for Life Laboratory (SciLifeLab) is run jointly by Uppsala University (UU), KTH Royal Institute of Technology, Karolinska Institutet (KI) and Stockholm University (SU). SciLifeLab brings together researchers across traditional boundaries and promotes collaboration with industry, healthcare, public research organisations and international partners. As a SciLifeLab Fellow, the successful candidate will be part of the dynamic SciLifeLab community, both locally in Uppsala and across Sweden as a whole. For information on the SciLifeLab Fellow programme, see https://www.scilifelab.se/contact/fellows/. SciLifeLab Fellows are also part of a broad national network of future academic leaders within SciLifeLab and the Wallenberg National Program for Data-Driven Life Science (DDLS), as well as the fellowship programme at the Wallenberg Centres for Molecular Medicine (WCMM), within the Program for Academic leaders in Life Science (PALS) network; see https://www.palsnetwork.se . SciLifeLab is now seeking a promising researcher to further strengthen the research environment in Uppsala. Placement will be within a department of the Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy and will be determined at the time of appointment. Description of the subject area Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) has emerged as one of the most serious global health threats. As drug-resistant pathogens spread, many of the advances in modern medicine – ranging from routine surgical procedures to cancer treatment and the care of premature babies – are at risk of being undermined. The rate at which antibiotics are ceasing to work due to resistance is alarming. Given the scale of this crisis, the World Health Organization has identified AMR as one of the highest-priority health issues. Research into AMR is well aligned with SciLifeLab’s areas of expertise, and a SciLifeLab Fellow in this field will further strengthen Uppsala’s position as a national and international hub for antibiotic development and translational innovations. This creates significant opportunities to accelerate research efforts and deepen our understanding of resistance mechanisms. AMR research encompasses, but is not limited to, the discovery and development of new antibiotics and research, diagnostics and existing treatments. Together, this research initiative forms a basis for combating AMR, strengthening global public health and enabling the development of new antibiotics. A SciLifeLab Fellow in AMR will therefore work within a rapidly expanding field of research with great potential to influence global health developments. Duties Research, teaching and administration. In addition to these, the duties include supervising PhD students in their research projects and participating in first- and second-cycle education at the department. They also include monitoring developments in antimicrobial resistance and broader societal developments that are relevant to the work of the University. Administrative duties and internal and external commissions of trust may be required. The position is intended to lead to the development of an independent research profile in the field of antimicrobial resistance. The successful candidate is expected to strengthen the University’s contribution to SciLifeLab (www.scilifelab.se). Period of appointment Employment as an associate senior lecturer is a six-year career-development position. However, if special reasons exist, the term of employment may be renewed for no more than two years. An associate senior lecturer may apply and be considered for promotion. To be considered for promotion to senior lecturer, a written application must be received by the Disciplinary Domain Board for Medicine and Pharmacy no later than six months before the appointment as associate senior lecturer ends. If the associate senior lecturer is assessed as suitable and meets the requirements for promotion, they shall be promoted and employed as a senior lecturer under a permanent contract. Qualifications According to Chapter 4, §4a of the Higher Education Ordinance, a person is qualified for appointment as an associate senior lecturer if they have obtained a PhD or have attained equivalent academic competence. According to §44a of the Guidelines and Assessment Criteria for Recruiting and Promoting Teachers at the Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy (GA), primary consideration shall be given to an applicant who has obtained a PhD or has attained equivalent academic competence no more than seven years prior to the closing date for applications. Furthermore, according to §5 of the Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University (AR), a general eligibility requirement for teaching staff is that they possess the personal qualities necessary to perform the duties of the position effectively. The applicant must have a documented ability to teach in Swedish or English. Upon promotion to a higher teaching position, the applicant must demonstrate adequate skills in both Swedish and English to be able to contribute to the University’s internal work. See §6 of the AR. Assessment criteria When selecting from among multiple qualified applicants, research expertise will be assigned greater weight than teaching expertise. Weight will also be given to collaborative expertise, demonstrated through a proven ability to establish national and international collaborations. When assessing research expertise, particular weight will be given to having a competitive research profile and the applicant’s potential to contribute to the future development in the field of antimicrobial resistance. Research expertise refers to research qualifications. When assessing research expertise, research quality will be the primary consideration. The scope of the research, particularly in terms of its depth and breadth, shall also be taken into account. Furthermore, consideration shall be given to the capacity to plan, initiate, lead and develop research and education at the doctoral level, the ability to acquire funding for research in competition, as well as the demonstrated capacity to interact with others both within academia and in the wider community. See §20 of the AR. See also §11 of Guidelines and Assessment Criteria for Recruiting and Promoting Teachers at the Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy (GA). Teaching expertise refers to teaching qualifications. When assessing teaching expertise, teaching quality will be the prime consideration. The scope of teaching experience, in terms of both breadth and depth, shall be afforded consideration. Furthermore, consideration shall be given to the capacity to plan, initiate, lead, and develop teaching, as well as the ability to connect research to teaching based on research in the subject at hand, subject didactics, as well as teaching and learning in higher education. Collaborative teaching capacity and the ability to interact with actors inside and outside the University in relation to issues of teaching and learning in higher education are also included in teaching expertise. See §22 of the AR. See also §12 of the GA. The applicant should have completed at least five weeks of training in teaching and learning in higher education relevant to the department/equivalent or have equivalent skills. If the applicant was unable to complete such a qualification prior to employment, the qualifying training in teaching and learning in higher education must be completed during the first two years of employment. See §39 of the AR. Assessment criteria, other expertise Administrative and management expertise are also significant to the position and will be assigned weight. The ability to collaborate with the wider community and to communicate information about research and development work will be taken into account. Administrative expertise is demonstrated through, for example, the ability to plan, organise and prioritise work in an efficient and appropriate manner, as well as the ability to specify and adhere to time frames. Such expertise includes overall activity planning; the ability to manage resources in a way that reflects operational priorities; and the ability to work in a structured manner and based on an awareness of goals and quality. (§28 of the AR). See also §13 of the GA. Management expertise is demonstrated through the ability to lead activities and staff, make decisions, take responsibility, motivate others and provide them with what they require for the effective achievement of shared goals. Expertise may also be demonstrated through the ability to coordinate the group; to help create a sense of involvement, participation and job satisfaction; and to deal with conflicts. (§30 of the AR). See also §13 of the GA. When assessing collaborative expertise, experience with and expertise in popular science work, editing and other activities related to the exchange of knowledge between the University and the outside world, as well as experience with innovation and entrepreneurship, shall be of significance. (§14 of the GA) In an overall assessment of the applicants’ qualifications, parental leave, part-time work due to childcare, trade union responsibilities, military service or similar activities shall be treated as work experience. (§94 of the AR). When the University appoints new teachers, it shall select the applicants who, following a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and expertise, are judged to have the best potential to perform and develop the duties concerned and to contribute to the positive development of the department/equivalent. (§4 of the AR). The gender equality aspect shall be applied in the appointment process if, following qualitative assessment, two applicants of different genders are found to have equivalent or near-equivalent qualifications and one of the genders is under-represented (accounts for less than 40 percent within the occupational category in question and at the workplace concerned). (§95 of the AR) All qualifications must be documented to enable assessment of both quality and scope. Other The position is linked to the SciLifeLab Fellow programme at Uppsala University, which provides core funding of SEK 15 million over six years. International experts may be involved in the assessment of submitted applications. In such a case, application documents written in Swedish may need to be sent to a translator contracted by the University. Links to relevant regulations and instructions Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University Guidelines and Assessment Criteria for Recruiting and Promoting Teachers at the Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy Career portfolios: Compilation Instructions and Assessment Guidelines for the Recruitment of Teachers, Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy About the position: Fixed-term appointment, maximum 6 years, full-time (100%). Start date by agreement. Location: Uppsala Further information about the position is available from Pernilla Åsenlöf, Dean of the Faculty of Medicine, pernilla.asenlöf@uu.se, 018-471 4768 or Anja Sandström, Dean of the Faculty of Pharmacy, anja.sandstrom@ilk.uu.se, 018-471 50 26 We welcome your application no later than 9 November 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2888 Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Special fixed-term employment Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2888 Last application date: 9 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=963089": {
      "title": "Researcher in Experimental Immunology",
      "description": "Researcher in Experimental Immunology - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Researcher in Experimental Immunology 2026-09-17 The Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology (IMBIM) at Uppsala University offers a broad, international environment for research and teaching. IMBIM conducts basic research in biochemistry, cell and molecular biology, tumor biology, comparative genetics, functional genomics, immunology, bacteriology, and virology. The department’s research is primarily basic, but its applications have clear connections to and significance for health and disease in both animals and humans. A more detailed description is available at Research – Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology – Uppsala University Tasks Main tasks are research on molecular mechanisms in the field of inflammatory skin diseases, including psoriasis and atopic dermatitis. In particular, the research will focus on various methods to study the role of mast cells in such diseases. Among other things, the work will include new methods to induce selective apoptosis in mast cells. The work will include culture of primary cells and several techniques to study the effect of different substances on skin mast cells, e.g., fluorescence microscopy, live imaging, flow cytometry, in vivo techniques and various cell biological and biochemical techniques. Qualification requirements Doctoral degree in immunology, molecular/cell biology or equivalent, with extensive experience from experimental laboratory work. The work requires documented experience in cell culture, in vivo techniques, as well as experience in various immunological and cell biology techniques such as flow cytometry, qPCR, Western blot, transfections, cell staining and microscopy. Prior experience in skin biology and/or mast cell biology is an advantage. The applicant must have the ability to work independently and be able to collaborate with other members of the group as well as with national and international partners. Very good knowledge of English, both spoken and written, is required. Personal qualities such as flexibility, accuracy and the ability to collaborate are valued. Selection Criteria When selecting among qualified applicants, particular emphasis will be placed on scientific competence. In this recruitment, the University will primarily consider the candidate who, following a comprehensive assessment of documented qualifications, competence, and skills, is deemed to have the best prerequisites to carry out and develop the relevant duties and contribute to the positive development of the department. About the Position The employment is a temporary position for six months, with an eventual possible opportunity for continued fixed-term employment. The position is full-time. Start date to be agreed upon. Location: Uppsala For further information regarding the position , please contact: Professor Gunnar Pejler, gunnar.pejler@imbim.uu.se and Professor Enikö Pivarcsi Sonkoly, eniko.sonkoly@medsci.uu.se Please submit your application latest by October 15, 2026. UFV-PA 2026/2745 Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Special fixed-term employment Pay: Individuell Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2745 Last application date: 15 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=970449": {
      "title": "Postdoc position in probabilistic methods for foundation and world models",
      "description": "Postdoc position in probabilistic methods for foundation and world models - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoc position in probabilistic methods for foundation and world models 2026-09-17 Are you interested in working with probabilistic machine learning for the next generation of AI models – uncertainty-aware foundation models, generative models and world models – with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a postdoctoral position at Uppsala University. The Department of Information Technology holds a leading position in both research and education at all levels. We are currently Uppsala University’s third largest department, have around 350 employees, including 120 teachers and 120 PhD students. Approximately 5,000 undergraduate students take one or more courses at the department each year. The department also participates in the Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems and Software Program ( WASP ). You can find more information about us on the Department of Information Technology website. The position is hosted by the Division of Scientific Computing (TDB), one of the world’s largest research environments in computational science, with large activities in areas such as machine learning, optimization, scientific software development and high-performance computing. The division is an important part of the eSSENCE e-science collaboration and of the Science for Life Laboratory ( SciLifeLab ) network, a national research infrastructure for life  sciences. The successful candidate will join the Scientific Machine Learning group at TDB and SciLifeLab. The group develops theory, methods and software for data-driven science, with a current focus on uncertainty quantification in large pre-trained models (vision-language models), generative models (flow matching, diffusion), simulation-based inference, and robust and active learning. The group has a wide network of collaborators and strong access to compute through national GPU systems (NAISS, e.g. Berzelius and Arrhenius) and local GPU infrastructure. Project description The position offers significant scientific freedom around the central theme of probabilistic methods for foundation models and world models: making them uncertainty-aware, calibrated, robust and useful for scientific decision-making, by tackling the challenging, open problems that matter most for how such models are used today. You may propose your own topic within the theme or start from one of the following directions: Uncertainty quantification, calibration and reliability of large pre-trained models Probabilistic generative models and world models Probabilistic machine learning for scientific discovery Don’t see your exact idea listed? We encourage bespoke proposals – outline your own research direction (max 2 pages) within the theme above. Duties Research, publication and presentation of results at international conferences, contributions to the group’s open-source software, and participation in the supervision of students. A limited amount of teaching may be included (max 20%). Requirements PhD degree in machine learning, computer science, scientific computing, mathematics, statistics or a related field, or a foreign degree equivalent to a PhD degree in machine learning, computer science, scientific computing, mathematics, statistics or a related field. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Priority will be given to applicants who have completed their degree no more than three years before the deadline for applications. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. Documented research experience in modern deep learning (e.g. generative models, Bayesian deep learning or large pre-trained models) and excellent programming skills in Python and a modern deep learning framework (e.g., PyTorch or JAX) are required. Excellent skills in spoken and written English are required. The candidate must clearly document a high degree of self-motivation in the application. Great emphasis will be placed on personal characteristics such as creativity, thoroughness, a structured approach to problem-solving, and the ability to work both independently and in a team. Additional qualifications Publications at top machine learning or computer vision conferences (NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, CVPR, AISTATS etc.) are highly meriting. Expertise in Bayesian methods, generative models, multimodal models, world models or simulation-based inference is meriting, as is experience with large-scale training on GPU clusters, open-source software development and applications in the life sciences. Teaching experience is considered a merit. This may include teaching, supervision, mentoring, course assistance, providing internal training, or other educational activities, within or outside higher education. In assessing such experience, particular consideration will be given to activities that support students' learning in computer science, information technology, or closely related subjects. The assessment will take the applicant's career stage into account, and extensive teaching experience is not expected. Application The application must contain: A curriculum vitae (CV), A copy of relevant grade documents (translated into Swedish or English), A list of publications, Up to five selected publications in electronic format A research statement describing your past and current research (max 1 page) and a proposal for future activities (max 1 page). Contact information for two references. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of two years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date 1 November 2026 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Associate Professor Prashant Singh, prashant.singh@scilifelab.uu.se; Head of Division Elisabeth Larsson,  elisabeth.larsson@it.uu.se. In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by Thursday October 15, 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2764. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science, Department of Information Technology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individual salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2764 Last application date: 15 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=970707": {
      "title": "PhD student in Chemistry with specialization in semi-solid electrolytes for lithium-ion batteries",
      "description": "PhD student in Chemistry with specialization in semi-solid electrolytes for lithium-ion batteries  - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student in Chemistry with specialization in semi-solid electrolytes for lithium-ion batteries 2026-09-17 The Department of Chemistry - Ångström conducts research and education in the chemistry field. The department has more than 270 employees and has a turnover of 300 million SEK. At the department's six programs, we conduct very successful research of a high international standard. We have a large number of externally funded research projects, often with international cooperation and we see continued good growth in our subject area. The department has education assignments in engineering programs and master's programs. More information is available on our website . The Structural Chemistry program at the Department of Chemistry – Ångström has for many years hosted an environment focused on research and development of materials and their applications within the energy storage area: the Ångström Advanced Battery Centre. We develop novel electrode and electrolyte materials, characterize them, evaluate and improve them with respect to battery performance, and study fundamental chemical processes and properties using both experimental and computational techniques. The research is, as such, both fundamental and applied. Duties We are looking for a motivated and ambitious student for developing semi-solid electrolytes and characterizing their implementation and performance in lithium-ion batteries. The project involves formulation of electrolytes, assembly and testing of battery devices. The project requires extensive use of characterization techniques including electrochemistry, spectroscopy, microscopy and structural characterization. The student will design, plan, and execute the experimental work, often in collaboration with colleagues, critically analyze and discuss the results, and disseminate the work orally at scientific conferences and written in the form of papers in peer-reviewed journals and the doctoral thesis. The doctoral studies also involve courses and possibly teaching or other departmental duties to a certain extent. Requirements To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must been awarded a second-cycle degree in chemistry, physics, chemical engineering or materials science, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or acquired essentially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. The candidate must have: very good oral and written proficiency in English. Highly motivated and able to work independently and as a part of a large team Knowledge and experience with electrochemistry and battery materials characterization Consideration will also be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant’s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. Additional qualifications It is desirable that applicants have educational or research experience in batteries, electrolytes and/or polymers. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 2027-01-04 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines. For further information about the position, please contact: Guiomar Hernández, guiomar.hernandez@kemi.uu.se Please submit your application by 20 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2775. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Chemistry - Ångström Laboratory Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2775 Last application date: 20 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=970239": {
      "title": "PhD student in bio-based battery electrolytes",
      "description": "PhD student in bio-based battery electrolytes - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student in bio-based battery electrolytes 2026-09-16 The Department of Chemistry - Ångström conducts research and education in the chemistry field. The department has more than 270 employees and has a turnover of 300 million SEK. At the department's six programs, we conduct very successful research of a high international standard. We have a large number of externally funded research projects, often with international cooperation and we see continued good growth in our subject area. The department has education assignments in engineering programs and master's programs. More information is available on our website . Department of Chemistry Ångström Laboratory The Structural Chemistry section at the Department of Chemistry – Ångström Laboratory has for many years hosted a research environment focused on the development of materials and their applications within the energy storage area: the Ångström Advanced Battery Centre. We develop novel electrode and electrolyte materials, characterize them, evaluate and improve them with respect to battery performance, and study fundamental chemical processes and properties using both experimental and computational techniques. The research is, as such, both fundamental and applied. Duties This project will target a more sustainable battery value chain through implementation of bio-based electrolytes, from renewable carbon feedstocks, in lithium- and sodium-ion batteries. The ultimate purpose is to reduce climate impact, improve safety, and decrease strategic dependence on fossil and externally sourced raw materials. Through the combined development of tailored bio-based electrolytes, the study of their performance with state-of-the-art electrode chemistries, and investigation of electrode-electrolyte interfaces, you will establish scientifically grounded design principles for sustainable electrolytes that meet industrial performance requirements. The main activities involved in the doctoral studies are in conducting experimental research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. You will also take third-cycle courses related to the research topics. The project will be carried out at Uppsala University in close collaboration with the project team and other colleagues at the Ångström Advanced Battery Centre. The work will mostly be to conduct experimental research into developing bio-based electrolytes for lithium- and sodium-ion batteries. This will generally include liquid electrolyte development, battery assembly, the use of various electrochemical techniques ( e.g. galvanostatic cycling, cyclic voltammetry, electrochemical impedance spectroscopy) and advanced characterisation methods ( e.g. X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy, scanning electron microscopy, infrared spectroscopy), both locally and at international large-scale facilities. You are expected to perform high-quality research as part of a team, with the aim of disseminating resulting works through high impact peer-reviewed journals, and at national and international conferences. Requirements To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must been awarded a second-cycle degree in chemistry, physics, materials science, or a closely related subject, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or acquired essentially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. To be considered for this position, you must have: a good working knowledge of battery energy storage systems, experience of working in an experimental laboratory environment, skills in high-quality academic writing (for example research project reports, thesis, or published articles), the capability to express themself clearly, document experimental work efficiently, and work together with others in a research environment, very good oral and written proficiency in English. Consideration will also be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant’s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. Additional qualifications The following qualifications may also be considered: previous experience in the research field of electrochemical energy storage, particularly batteries, is desirable, e.g. through a master thesis project. previous experience working with materials characterisation, particularly for battery interfaces, is an advantage. knowledge of organic chemistry, particularly related to organic synthesis and properties of organic molecules, is an advantage. good knowledge of data curation and plotting, electronic laboratory notebooks, Python or similar, are merits. excellent grades from second-cycle education are a merit. Application Procedure The application must contain the following: CV Copies of degree certificates and grade transcripts Master’s thesis or equivalent (final/draft) Contact details of two references Other documentation in support of the requirements or qualifications About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 2026-11-01 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines . For further information about the position, please contact: Andy Naylor, andy.naylor@kemi.uu.se Please submit your application by 16 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2757. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Chemistry - Ångström Laboratory Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Fast lönestege Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2757 Last application date: 16 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=970288": {
      "title": "Postdoc position in organic synthesis of battery electrolyte solvents",
      "description": "Postdoc position in organic synthesis of battery electrolyte solvents - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoc position in organic synthesis of battery electrolyte solvents 2026-09-16 The Department of Chemistry - Ångström conducts research and education in the chemistry field. The department has more than 270 employees and has a turnover of 300 million SEK. At the department's six programs, we conduct very successful research of a high international standard. We have a large number of externally funded research projects, often with international cooperation and we see continued good growth in our subject area. The department has education assignments in engineering programs and master's programs. More information is available on our website . (https://kemi.uu.se/angstrom/?languageId=1). The Structural Chemistry section at the Department of Chemistry – Ångström Laboratory has for many years hosted a research environment focused on the development of materials and their applications within the energy storage area: the Ångström Advanced Battery Centre. We develop novel electrode and electrolyte materials, characterize them, evaluate and improve them with respect to battery performance, and study fundamental chemical processes and properties using both experimental and computational techniques. The research is, as such, both fundamental and applied. Work duties The main research activities will be to design and synthesise bio-based solvents for use in sustainable electrolytes for lithium- and sodium-ion batteries. This work is part of a project that will target a more sustainable battery value chain through design of electrolyte solvents from renewable carbon feedstocks, thereby reducing climate impact, improving safety, and decreasing strategic dependence on fossil and externally sourced raw materials. Through the combined design and development of tailored bio-based solvents, you will establish scientifically grounded design principles for sustainable electrolytes that meet industrial performance requirements. The main duty involved in a post-doctoral position is to conduct research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. The project will be carried out at Uppsala University in close collaboration with colleagues at the Ångström Advanced Battery Centre. The main tasks are the design and synthesis of bio-based solvent molecules, characterisation of the products by, for example NMR, FTIR, UV-Vis, and GC-MS, and determination of physicochemical properties relevant to electrolyte solvents, e.g. boiling point and viscosity. You are expected to work together with others who are testing the applicability and electrochemical performance of bio-based electrolytes in relevant battery systems. Within the project, you will also participate in dialogues and workshops with industry partners and international collaborators to inform the development of the electrolyte solvents. The postdoc is expected to perform high-quality research as part of a team, with the aim of disseminating resulting works through high impact peer-reviewed journals, and at national and international conferences. There may also be possibilities of building further collaborations in the research area, supervising students conducting degree projects, and seeking external research or travel grants. Requirements PhD degree in chemistry, chemical engineering or a closely related subject, or a foreign degree equivalent to a PhD degree. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Those who have obtained a PhD degree within the three years prior to the application deadline are primarily considered for the employment. The starting point of the three-year time period is the application deadline. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. The assessment of applications is based primarily on the applicant's ability to conduct independent research based on scientific skill. Greater importance is attached to the quality of individual scientific work, than to the amount of publications. To be considered for this position, you must have: Experience of synthesising and characterising organic solvents that are relevant to battery electrolytes is essential. Skills are required in characterisation techniques including NMR and GC-MS and the interpretation of data from such techniques. It is necessary to demonstrate the ability to work together with others, to publish high quality scientific publications, and to have presented work at internationally-relevant conferences. The candidate must have excellent capabilities in written and oral English. Consideration will be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant’s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. Desirable qualifications The following qualifications may also be considered: Previous experience in organic synthesis with consideration to sustainability and fossil-free precursors is an advantage. A PhD topic or other previous experiences involving battery electrolytes is desirable, but not essential. Familiarity with other aspects of battery research or industry is likewise advantageous. Experience of building up dedicated laboratory apparatus for a project is desirable. Good knowledge of data curation and plotting, electronic laboratory notebooks, Python or similar, are merits. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of 2 years according to central collective agreement, with the possibility of an extension of up to 1 year. Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 2026-10-26 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Andy Naylor, andy.naylor@kemi.uu.se Please submit your application by 16 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2760. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Chemistry - Ångström Laboratory Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2760 Last application date: 16 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=969552": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in simulation-based inference for particle physics",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in simulation-based inference for particle physics - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in simulation-based inference for particle physics 2026-09-15 Are you interested in working with machine learning and simulation-based inference for searches for dark matter (or other \"invisible\" new physics signals) at the Large Hadron Collider, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a postdoctoral position at Uppsala University. The Department of Information Technology holds a leading position in both research and education at all levels. We are currently Uppsala University’s third largest department, have around 350 employees, including 120 teachers and 120 PhD students. Approximately 5,000 undergraduate students take one or more courses at the department each year. You can find more information about us on the Department of Information Technology website. The position is hosted by the Division of Scientific Computing (TDB) within the Department of Information Technology. As one of the world’s largest focused research environments in Computational Science, the research and education has a unique breadth, with large activities in areas such as numerical analysis, mathematical modelling, development and analysis of algorithms, machine learning, optimization, scientific software development and high-performance computing. The division is also an important part of the eSSENCE strategic collaboration on e-science and of the Science for Life Laboratory ( SciLifeLab ) network, a national research infrastructure with a mandate to enable cutting-edge life science research in Sweden. The successful candidate will join the Scientific Machine Learning group at TDB and SciLifeLab (Associate Professor Prashant Singh), which develops methods and software for simulation-based inference, generative models and robust machine learning, together with the Theoretical Particle Physics group at the Department of Physics and Astronomy (Professor Stefano Moretti), which works on beyond-the-Standard-Model and dark-matter phenomenology and is a member of the CMS experiment at CERN. Together, the groups offer an international environment with a wide network of collaborators, generous support for conference travel, and access to national HPC resources (NAISS) and local GPU infrastructure. This Postdoc position is part of the eSSENCE graduate school in data-intensive science. The school addresses the challenge of data-intensive science both from the foundational methodological perspective and from the perspective of data-driven science applications. It is an arena where experts in computational science, data science and data engineering (systems and methodology) work closely together with researchers in (data-driven) sciences, industry and society to accelerate data-intensive scientific discovery. eSSENCE is a strategic collaborative research programme in e-science between three Swedish universities with a strong tradition of excellent e-science research: Uppsala University, Lund University and Umeå University. In this project we envision a novel cross-faculty collaboration between the Division of Scientific Computing and the Department of Physics and Astronomy, where new methodology for simulation-based inference is developed and applied directly in realistic collider analyses. The postdoc will be hosted at TDB, co-supervised by both groups, and will work at the interface of scientific computing, machine learning and particle physics. Project description Searches for dark matter (or other \"invisible\" new physics signals) at the Large Hadron Collider (LHC) compare high-dimensional collision data against detailed simulations whose likelihood cannot be evaluated, only sampled. Simulation-based inference (SBI) addresses this by training neural networks, such as flow-matching generative models, on simulated events. The project aims to develop efficient, robust and calibrated SBI methods for such searches that account for event selection and systematic uncertainties, and to demonstrate them on realistic searches at scale on national HPC resources. The project will primarily use Monte Carlo simulated data, but there is also the possibility of working with real open data from the ATLAS and/or CMS experiments. The methods are general and applicable well beyond particle physics. Duties Research within the project described above, including method development, implementation, large-scale computational experiments on national HPC resources, and publication at machine learning and physics venues. The duties also include presenting results at international conferences, contributing to the group’s open-source software, actively participating in the activities of the eSSENCE graduate school, and taking part in the supervision of students. A limited amount of teaching may be included (max 20%). Requirements PhD degree in machine learning, scientific computing, statistics, physics or a related field, or a foreign degree equivalent to a PhD degree in machine learning, scientific computing, statistics, physics or a related field. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Priority will be given to applicants who have completed their degree no more than three years before the deadline for applications. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. Documented experience in machine learning, in particular deep generative models and/or probabilistic modelling, and excellent programming skills in Python and a modern deep learning framework (e.g., PyTorch or JAX) are required. Excellent skills in spoken and written English are required. The candidate must clearly document a high degree of self-motivation in the application. Great emphasis will be placed on personal characteristics such as a high level of creativity, thoroughness, a structured approach to problem-solving, and the ability to work both independently and as part of an interdisciplinary team. Additional qualifications Experience in simulation-based or likelihood-free inference, normalizing flows, flow matching or diffusion models is meriting. Experience in particle physics, in particular with collider simulation tools (e.g., MadGraph, Pythia, Delphes), statistical analysis of LHC data or beyond-the-Standard-Model phenomenology, is meriting. Experience with large-scale training on GPU and HPC systems, with design of experiments and active learning, with open-source software development, and with interdisciplinary collaboration is meriting. Publications at top machine learning conferences (ICLR, ICML, NeurIPS, AISTATS, etc.) or in leading physics journals are advantageous. Teaching experience is considered a merit. This may include teaching, supervision, mentoring, course assistance, providing internal training, or other educational activities, within or outside higher education. In assessing such experience, particular consideration will be given to activities that support students' learning in computer science, information technology, or closely related subjects. The assessment will take the applicant's career stage into account, and extensive teaching experience is not expected. Application The application must contain: A curriculum vitae (CV), A copy of relevant grade documents (translated into Swedish or English), A list of publications, Up to five selected publications in electronic format A research statement describing your past and current research (max 1 page) and a proposal for future activities (max 1 page). Contact information for two references. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of two years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date 1 November 2026 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Associate Professor Prashant Singh, prashant.singh@scilifelab.uu.se; Professor Stefano Moretti,  stefano.moretti@physics.uu.se; Head of Division Elisabeth Larsson,  elisabeth.larsson@it.uu.se. In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by Thursday October 15, 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2734. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science, Department of Information Technology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individual salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2734 Last application date: 15 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=937704": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Biochemistry",
      "description": "Associate Professor in Biochemistry - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Associate Professor in Biochemistry 2026-09-11 Do you want to be part of an outstanding research environment in protein biochemistry and move your research forward at Sweden’s largest faculty of science and technology? We are now looking for an Associate Professor in Biochemistry specialising in Protein Biochemistry who wishes to be involved in developing and strengthening our research and education at the Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences, Uppsala University. Biochemistry is a core area at the Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences and a central part of the Faculty of Science and Technology’s life science profile. You will be part of the Biochemistry programme, which conducts outstanding research in the area of understanding the chemical and molecular principles that govern biological systems, with particular emphasis on the structure, function, dynamics, interactions, evolution and catalytic mechanisms of proteins. The recruitment is strategically important for maintaining and renewing internationally competitive research and education in protein biochemistry. The field is developing rapidly through the integration of advanced experimental methodology, large-scale data, AI-based models and new concepts for understanding, designing and modulating protein function. The successful candidate will contribute to strengthening the programme’s established profile in molecular recognition, protein structure and dynamics, enzymatic mechanisms, protein engineering and/or interactomics, while also helping to develop new areas of research. The position offers excellent opportunities to build an internationally leading research group in a strong and collaborative environment. The successful candidate will be able to develop synergies with existing activities in biochemistry, structural biology, biophysics, enzymology, interaction analysis, protein engineering and computational molecular life science. We are based at the Biomedical centre (BMC). The research environment provides extensive opportunities for collaboration. Within the department, there are close links to analytical and organic chemistry, the NMR Centre and the Centre for Chemical Mechanism of Life. Within the faculty, there are strong connections to the Department of Cell and Molecular Biology. The position also offers excellent opportunities for collaboration with SciLifeLab, the Faculty of Pharmacy and the Faculty of Medicine. You can read more about the research and education carried out at the Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences and the Faculty of Science and Technology here: https://www.uu.se/en/department/chemistry-for-life-sciences/research/biochemistry Institutionen för kemi inom livsvetenskaperna – Uppsala universitet Subject area The subject area of the position is experimental biochemistry, with specialisation in protein biochemistry. Protein biochemistry concerns the molecular and chemical principles that govern the structure, function, dynamics, interactions, evolution and catalytic mechanisms of proteins. The subject area includes experimental and/or computational studies of proteins and their roles in biological systems. Relevant areas may include molecular recognition, protein structure and dynamics, enzymology, protein engineering, protein design, directed evolution of protein function, interactomics and/or multimodal analysis. The position is intended to strengthen and renew research and education in protein biochemistry and to contribute to the continued development of molecular life science at the Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences and the Faculty of Science and Technology. Duties You will work with: research. Research includes to conduct independent, internationally competitive research in biochemistry. This includes establishing and leading a research group, publishing in high-quality scientific journals, actively applying for external grants, and contributing to the scientific renewal of the biochemistry programme. The research may involve advanced experimental biochemistry, molecular interaction analysis, interactomics, enzymology, protein structure and dynamics, protein engineering, rational protein and enzyme design, directed protein evolution, biologics, targeted protein degradation or stabilisation and/or sustainable biocatalysis. teaching. Teaching includes responsibility for courses, course administration and supervision of doctoral students. Teaching includes to teach, in English and Swedish, at first-cycle, second-cycle and third-cycle levels in biochemistry and related areas, with particular responsibility for teaching in protein biochemistry, enzymology, protein structure and function, molecular interactions and biochemical methodology. If you are initially unable to teach in Swedish, Swedish-language training aimed at achieving this proficiency will be included in your duties. The duties also include supervision of degree projects and doctoral students, development of courses and teaching materials, and linking current research to teaching. administration. Participate in the general academic duties of the Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences. This includes serving on committees, taking on responsibilities beyond your own research and teaching assignments, contributing to the evaluation and development of teaching and research activities, working collaboratively with colleagues, and providing support and constructive feedback to colleagues. keeping up to date in your subject area and following developments in society that are relevant to your work at Uppsala University. In choosing between eligible candidates, emphasis will primarily be given to both research and teaching expertise, which will be accorded equal weight. In addition, attention will be given to administrative, and management expertise. Qualifications required You must have: a PhD in biochemistry or another closely related subject area of relevance to protein biochemistry research. research expertise in protein biochemistry. The applicant must have demonstrated the ability to conduct high-quality independent research of relevance to the subject area, including a strong publication record and a clear research profile in experimental protein biochemistry or closely related areas. In addition to academic qualifications, research qualifications from other activities may also be taken into account, such as development of technology and capacity for innovation. teaching expertise in biochemistry or closely related subject areas, with relevance to protein biochemistry, including demonstrated ability to plan, carry out, evaluate and develop teaching at university level. In addition to academic qualifications, educational and instructional qualifications from other activities may also be taken into account, such as supervision, internal training or mentoring programmes. completed at least ten weeks of teacher training for higher education of relevance to the organisation and its activities, or be considered to have acquired the equivalent knowledge. The required training for teachers in higher education may be completed during the first two years of employment if there are special reasons. a documented ability to teach in Swedish or English. an ability to work with other people and otherwise meet the demands of suitability required to perform the duties well. an ability to link research to teaching, based on the subject concerned, subject didactics and teaching and learning in higher education, and to interact on issues of teaching and learning in higher education with actors within and outside the University. a documented ability to obtain external grants. documented skills and expertise in experimental protein biochemistry, such as molecular interaction analysis, enzymology, protein structure and dynamics, protein engineering, directed evolution, protein or enzyme design, and biochemical method development. documented ability to develop and lead research activities, including supervision of students and early-career researchers. research and teaching expertise or other professional expertise. The teaching expertise, research expertise and professional expertise must be relevant to the subject area and the duties that the position involves. Other desirable/valuable qualifications It is valuable if you have: research expertise that complements and strengthens existing activities within biochemistry, structural biology, biophysics, enzymology, interaction analysis, protein engineering and computational molecular life science. research expertise in AI-/machine-learning-supported protein analysis or design. demonstrated scientific impact. documented ability to initiate and develop interdisciplinary collaborations within academia and with external partners documented ability to communicate research and teaching to students, researchers, stakeholders and the wider community. documented administrative expertise. Administrative proficiency includes the ability to plan, organise and prioritise work, and to work in a structured manner with due attention to quality and objectives. documented management expertise. Developing, coordinating and leading operations and staff. For more information on assessment and assessment criteria, see the Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University and the Faculty of Science and Technology’s Guidelines for the Appointement and Promotion of Teachers. All qualifications must be documented in a manner that makes it possible to assess both their quality and their scope. In this recruitment, the University will give primary consideration to the candidate who, following a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and expertise, is judged to have the best potential to perform and develop the relevant duties and to contribute to the positive development of the department/equivalent. Application Parental leave, part-time work due to childcare, trade union responsibilities, military service or similar activities are treated as work experience and should be listed in the CV. Instructions for applications for employment About the position: This is an open-ended appointment (a probationary period may apply). The position is full-time(100%). Starting date August 1st 2027 or as agreed. Place of work: Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences, BMC, Uppsala University, Uppsala Further information about the position is available from: Professor Ylva Ivarsson, +46-18-471 4038, ylva.ivarsson@kemi.uu.se We look forward to receiving your application by November 20 2026, UFV-PA 2026/1715. In the event of any disagreement between the English and the Swedish versions of this announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. We offer you Sweden offers good working conditions, including comprehensive social benefits such as generous family-focused policies that make healthcare, childcare, and children’s education available and highly affordable. At Uppsala University, we offer the opportunity for new international staff to learn Swedish through our language courses. If you have family, they will get new contacts and support through the Uppsala International Citizen hub. If you are an international candidate, you will find a lot of information about working and living in Sweden at http://www.uu.se/joinus . Uppsala University’s tenure track career system entitles senior lecturers/associate professors to be considered for promotion to full professor. The University offers support for developing as a researcher and university teacher, leadership development, and patent and innovation support. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Chemistry for life sciences Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Permanent position Pay: Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/1715 Last application date: 20 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=964762": {
      "title": "Doctoral (Phd) position in the photophysics in 2D quantum materials",
      "description": "Doctoral (Phd) position in the photophysics in 2D quantum materials - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Doctoral (Phd) position in the photophysics in 2D quantum materials 2026-09-09 Admission to Doctoral (PhD) Studies in the subject Engineering Sciences with specialization in Solid State Physics. at the Division of Solid State Physics, Department of Materials Science and Engineering, Uppsala University Join us! About the Department The Department of Materials Science and Engineering aims to be an environment for successful and valuable research and education with a focus on materials science solutions for important societal challenges. Our department is an exciting workplace with research in a broad technology-related area, from basic research to large-scale applied research, and close contacts with students through the department's involvement in engineering and master's programs. Our research and teaching are conducted within seven divisions with different research focuses, as well as a division that provides support and service. The department is an international place to work, and has around 230 active co-workers. Read more about us here About the division The Division of Solid State Physics is part of the Department of Materials Science and Engineering, Ångström Laboratory. At the division, we do both basic and application-oriented research that is related to energy and environmental aspects as well as life science via our different research areas. Most commonly, we investigate physical and chemical properties of nanomaterials and compounds, whether they will be used as coatings for smart windows, for gas sensors, photocatalytic coatings, and spintronics, or for biomagnetic applications or to create new magnetic materials for environmentally friendly energy technologies. Read more about us here Project description The study and exploration of two-dimensional (2D) quantum materials, such as transition metal dichalcogenides (TMDs), has gained significant attention over the past few decades for their use in optoelectronics. Despite this interest, the photophysical properties of these materials and the physics of defects within these materials, introduced via different exfoliation methods, are not well understood. The overall goal of this project is to deepen the fundamental understanding of defect physics and provide fresh insights into the hotly debated topic of 2D material defect passivation, leveraging advanced vibration spectroscopies, time-resolved optical spectroscopy and microscopy for the first time. Duties The main duty for a doctoral student is to devote themselves to their research studies which includes participating in research projects and PhD courses. The work duties can also include teaching and other departmental duties (no more than 20%). Being a PhD student means independently running projects within a specific subject. You collaborate on an ongoing basis with other doctoral students and researchers to create results within various projects and have one or more supervisors for support during your doctoral studies. However, you work independently to a great amount, e.g. by working in a laboratory environment and writing articles for journals and for results for your doctoral thesis. Usually, some form of half-time seminar is included after about half of the doctoral studies. When you are admitted to doctoral studies, you are offered employment as a doctoral student. A position as a doctoral student at Uppsala University corresponds to full-time PhD education for four years. Read more about being a Doctoral student here . You will be responsible for conducting advanced spectroscopic investigations of 2D quantum materials, such as Raman, photoluminescence (PL), transient absorption spectroscopies, and X-ray-based spectroscopies. You will design, perform, and analyze experiments aimed at understanding the exciton dynamics of 2D materials via different exfoliation methods and the mechanisms of defect passivation. Additional responsibilities include the writing of scientific manuscripts, presentation of research findings at internal meetings and international conferences, and active participation in collaborative discussions within the research group. Eligibility requirements To meet the general entry requirements for doctoral studies, the applicant must have completed a degree at second-cycle level, completed at least 240 credits of higher education studies, of which at least 60 credits are at second-cycle level including an independent project of at least 15 credits, or otherwise acquired substantially equivalent knowledge. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100) chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines. Requirements Master’s degree in physics, chemistry, or a related field, or other education considered equivalent to these qualifications. Successfully completed relevant courses in Solid State Physics or Physical Chemistry We require good oral and written skills in English. Additional qualifications Basic knowledge and skills in 2D material characterization are valued. Experience with transient absorption spectroscopy is particularly meritorious. Likewise, experience with programming in MATLAB, Python, or similar for data analysis is highly valued. Great emphasis is put on personal qualities such as the ability to independently plan and carry out work. You have a good ability to work towards set goals and you work focused to achieve them. In this, you have an ability to focus, even during periods of high workload. You have good communication skills, where through this quality you cooperate well with others. You also have a good ability to write academic text. Furthermore, you need to be structured and able to work efficiently both individually and in groups. Your application must include A short cover letter (max 2 pages)  in which you describe yourself, why you want to do a PhD and why you are suitable for this position. CV (max 2 pages) A certified copy of your master's degree and your course grades. Copies (or drafts) of your master's thesis and other documents, such as publications, that you wish to refer to. Names and contact details of at least two contact persons who have agreed to be references for you, with any additional letters of recommendation. It must also be stated what relationship you have had with the respective referent. The application should be written in English. We will continuously read applications and call for interviews. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 2027-02-01 or as agreed upon. Placement: Uppsala Salary: Doctoral students at Uppsala University are covered by a doctoral salary ladder in accordance with the applicable local collective agreement. The first three years, the salary is determined based on the number of active years and then based on progression of the studies. Follow this link to read more. For further information about the position, please contact: Zhaojun Li, zhaojun.li@angstrom.uu.se Please submit your application by 20 October 2026 , UFV-PA 2026/2594 Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Materials Science and Engineering Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Lön enligt lokalt kollektivavtal för doktorander Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2594 Last application date: 20 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=967249": {
      "title": "PhD-student in Evolutionary and Ecological Genetics",
      "description": "PhD-student in Evolutionary and Ecological Genetics - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD-student in Evolutionary and Ecological Genetics 2026-09-09 Do you want to conduct frontier research in an outstanding environment within evolutionary biology at Sweden’s largest faculty of science and technology? The Department of Ecology and Genetics at Uppsala University conducts world-leading research in biology, spanning from molecules to ecosystems and global biodiversity patterns. We are now looking to recruit a PhD student who wishes to develop their research career together with us. The Department of Ecology and Genetics (IEG) at the Evolutionary Biology Center (EBC) is an international environment with staff that conducts research to understand ecological and evolutionary processes across all levels of biological organization. IEG provides access to advanced national and local research infrastructures, including free super computing resources (NAISS) and the latest molecular technologies and sequencing platforms (SciLifeLab platforms) . IEG hosts a Climate Lab with controlled environmental chambers and greenhouses, a state-of-the-art molecular lab, and animal rearing facilities. PhD-students at IEG can join the PhD school which provides ample opportunities for networking on and off campus with PhD-students from the other two biology departments at Uppsala University (The Department of Organismal Biology, and the Department of Cellular and Molecular Biology). The position is offered by the research program in Animal Ecology at IEG. The program’s current research spans population- and conservation-genomics and quantitative- and evolutionary genetics, evolutionary ecology, behavioral ecology, and macroecology. Further information about the Animal Ecology Program can be found here. Project description A central question in evolutionary biology is whether evolution is repeatable, and whether the same genes contribute to repeated phenotypic adaptations. This question has important implications for predicting genetic responses to changing environments. This project aims to integrate mechanistic insights about phenotypic adaptation with genomic data to understand how species evolve adaptations to changes in their environment. The project will leverage data from a large-scale Evolve-and-Resequence experiment in a cosmopolitan insect pest, the seed beetle Callosobruchus maculatus. This unique system allows us to study the roles of determinism and chance in local adaptation and the evolution of a species’ ecological niche. Extensive phenotypic, RNA-seq, and DNA pool-seq data are available from multiple time points in the experiment, which is still ongoing. Several other C. maculatus strains sampled across its global distribution and closely related seed beetle species are available in the host lab. This provides opportunities for comparative genomics and additional experiments and data collection to further develop the project. Duties The PhD project will involve a combination of experimental work and bioinformatic analysis, with emphasis on the latter. The exact balance between tasks may depend on the candidate's interests and the project's development. PhD students at the Institute of Ecology and Genetics (IEG) have the option to engage in teaching and to develop their pedagogic CV by taking courses. The type and level of teaching will depend on availability and the student's interests but cannot exceed 20% full-time employment. The position and funding is extended by the time the student has engaged in teaching. The PhD candidate will work with the main supervisor David Berger and with the co-supervisor, SciLifeLab fellow Dr. Gabriela Montejo-Kovacevich, both at IEG. Qualifications required To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must: hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in Evolutionary Biology, Ecology, Bioinformatics, or a related field, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or have acquired equivalent knowledge in some other way (e.g. extensive research experience). Candidates who have not yet completed their degree but are expected to meet the degree requirements before the start date are encouraged to apply. The ideal applicant should also: Have a grasp of key concepts in ecology and evolutionary biology/genetics. Have experience with programming and scripting. Be highly motivated and curious and thrive in a collaborative environment. Be able to take responsibility for carrying out and finishing independent tasks and projects. Candidates must be able to express themselves at a high level in spoken as well as written English. Additional Qualifications Some of the following skills are desirable: Experience with statistical analyses applied to quantitative genetic or population genomic data. Experience working with bioinformatic pipelines using computer servers and clusters. Experimental work, such as experience working with experimental evolution or genetic strains. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 §7. Scope of employment: full-time (100%), for 4-years. Starting date: flexible start date in 2027. Placement: Uppsala University. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines. Instructions for the application The application must include: A cover letter describing yourself, your research interests, why you want to pursue a PhD, and why you are suitable for this specific position and project (maximum 2 pages). CV. A brief description of your education. A copy of your master's degree and course transcripts, as well as a copy of your master's thesis. Names and contact details of at least two references (email and phone number). Any publications. For further information about the position, please contact Associate Professor, David Berger, david.berger@ebc.uu.se You are welcome to submit your application no later than 1 November, 2026. UFV-PA 2026/2654. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it is like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Ecology and Genetics Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: The salary is set in accordance with the established salary scale for doctoral students Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2654 Last application date: 1 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=909639": {
      "title": "Professor in Medical Bacteriology",
      "description": "Professor in Medical Bacteriology - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Professor in Medical Bacteriology 2026-09-04 The Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology (IMBIM) at Uppsala University offers a broad, international environment for research and teaching in a creative and open atmosphere. Research at the department is conducted within three interacting sections: Biochemistry and Cancer, Infection and Immunity, and Genetics and Genomics. IMBIM provides extensive opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration with leading research environments at Uppsala University, including the Uppsala Antibiotic Center, ENABLE-2, and the SciLifeLab research infrastructure. IMBIM will lead a new national strategic research area in antimicrobial resistance, which will be established later this year. Description of the subject area This subject area covers antimicrobial resistance, bacterial pathogenesis, host-pathogen interactions, or bacterial physiology. We welcome candidates with expertise in molecular biology, biochemistry, genetics, infection biology, and large-scale molecular methods, including genomics, proteomics, metabolomics, or microbiome research. Duties The successful candidate will have overall responsibility for research and doctoral education within the field of Medical Bacteriology, as well as supervision and teaching at first, second and third cycle levels. The position includes leading an active international research group in the field, and contributing to the positive development of research and education within the subject area in collaboration with the Faculty's researchers and teachers. Administrative duties, as well as internal and external positions of trust, may be included in the position. The position also includes disseminating information about research and development activities. The duties further include following developments within the candidate's own field and developments in society at large that are of relevance to the work of the University. Qualifications A person eligible for appointment as professor is one who has demonstrated both scholarly and teaching competence (Chapter 4, Section 3 of the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance). A general eligibility requirement in Section 5 of the Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University (AR) is that the applicant must have the ability to cooperate and otherwise meet the requirements for suitability needed to perform the duties well. The research expertise must have been demonstrated by independent research efforts and by the applicant's qualifications in an international perspective maintaining a very high quality. The applicant shall have demonstrated skill in the planning, initiation, leadership and development of research and the ability to obtain research grants in competition, as well as well-documented skills in supervising doctoral studies. The applicant's contribution to the international and national academic community shall be assessed on the basis of the quality and scope of academic publication, among other aspects. The requirements on the acquisition of international qualifications shall be assessed with due consideration for the nature and specific conditions of the subject. (AR Section 31). Pedagogical expertise must have been demonstrated through substantial qualifications in education in accordance with Section 22 of the AR. Furthermore, the applicant shall demonstrate well-documented skills in supervision at the first, second and third cycle levels.Completion of relevant academic teacher training, comprising a minimum of ten weeks, or the equivalent is a prerequisite in order for the applicant to be considered to possess the necessary teaching skills. If special reasons exist, the successful candidate who does not have training in teaching and learning in higher education may undergo such training during the first two years of employment. Academic teacher training shall include doctoral supervisor training. (AR Section 32). The applicant must have documented ability to teach in Swedish or English. See AR Section 6. Assessment criteria In selecting qualified applicants, greater importance will be placed on research expertise than on teaching expertise. However, a balanced assessment will be made so that an applicant with significantly greater teaching expertise can be ranked ahead of an applicant with a slight advantage in terms of research expertise. Research expertise refers to qualifications as a researcher. In the assessment of research expertise, research quality shall be the primary consideration. The scope of research, particularly in terms of depth and breadth, will also be assigned significance. Furthermore, consideration will be given to the ability to plan, initiate, lead and develop research and education at the doctoral level, the ability to secure research funding competitively, and the ability to engage with the wider society through research. (AR Section 20) Cf. Section 3 of the Guidelines and Assessment Criteria for Recruitment and Promotion within the Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy (GA). Pedagogical expertise refers to qualifications in teaching and learning. In the assessment of teaching expertise, quality shall be the primary consideration. Scope, both in terms of breadth and depth, shall also be considered. In addition, the ability to plan, initiate, lead and develop education and teaching, as well as the ability to link education to research are assigned significance. Teaching expertise includes the ability to interact with stakeholders within and outside the University on issues related to learning and teaching in higher education, (AR Section 22) Cf. Section 4 GA. Assessment criteria; other proficiency Applicants must demonstrate scientific excellence in experimental approaches, experience of interdisciplinary collaboration, and a strong track record in supervision and teaching. Administrative and leadership skills are important qualifications for the position and will be given weight in the assessment. The ability to engage with the wider community, as well as to communicate research and development activities, will also be taken into consideration. Administrative expertise is demonstrated through, for example, the capacity to plan, organise and prioritise work in a suitable and effective manner, as well as the ability to specify and adhere to time frames. This form of expertise includes overall work planning; ability to manage resources in a way that reflects operational priorities; and ability to work in a structured manner and on the basis of an awareness of goals and quality. See also sections 28 AR and section 5 GA. Management expertise is demonstrated through ability to lead operations and staff, make decisions, assume responsibility, motivate others and provide them with what they require for the effective achievement of common objectives. Ability to coordinate a group and to help generate a sense of commitment, enhance participation and enjoyment of work, and ability to deal with conflicts, are further examples of how expertise is demonstrated. See also sections 30 AR and section 5 GA. When assessing collaboration expertise, importance will be attached to experience and demonstrated ability in public outreach and science communication, editorial work, and other activities relating to knowledge exchange between the University and the wider community, as well as experience of innovation and entrepreneurship. (GA Section 6). In an overall assessment of the applicant's qualifications, parental leave, part-time work due to childcare, trade union responsibilities, military service or similar activities are to be treated as work experience. (AR Section 94). When the University appoints new teachers, it must select the applicants who, following a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and expertise, are judged to have the best potential to perform and develop the relevant duties and to contribute to the positive development of the department. (AR Section 4). The gender equality aspect must be applied in an appointment process if it is evident following a qualitative assessment that two applicants of different gender have equal or approximately equal qualifications and if one gender is underrepresented (constitutes less than 40% of those in the occupational category in question and at the workplace concerned). (AR Section 95). All qualifications must be documented so that both quality and degree can be assessed. During the evaluation of submitted applications, international referees may be used. In this event, the University may need to send applications that are written in Swedish to a qualified translator. In the event of any disagreement between the English and the Swedish versions of this announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Links to relevant regulations and guidelines Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University Guidelines and assessment criteria for recruiting and promoting teachers at the Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy Career Portfolios. Instructions for compiling qualifications and guidelines for qualifications assessment in connection with recruitment of teachers, Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy Welcome to submit your application, no later than the 31st of October, UFV-PA 2026/632 Trade union representatives: Saco-S, saco-s@uu.se; Seko, seko@uadm.uu.se; ST (OFR/S), ofr@uu.se. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy, Faculty of Medicine, Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Permanent position Pay: Individual salary negotiation applies Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/632 Last application date: 31 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=961348": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in brain tumor biology and treatment resistance",
      "description": "Research Assistant in brain tumor biology and treatment resistance - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Research Assistant in brain tumor biology and treatment resistance 2026-09-02 The Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology at Uppsala University has a broad research profile with strong research groups focusing on cancer, genetic and autoimmune diseases. A fundamental idea at the department is to stimulate translational research and thereby promote closer interactions between medical research and health care. Research is presently organized in six research programs: Cancer Precision Medicine, Cancer Immunotherapy, Genomics and Neurobiology, Molecular Tools and Functional Genomics, Neuro-Oncology and Neurodegeneration and Vascular Biology. Departmental activities are also integrated with the units for Oncology, Clinical Genetics, Clinical Immunology, Clinical Pathology, and Hospital Physics at Uppsala University Hospital. The department has teaching assignments in several education programs, including Master Programs, at the Faculty of Medicine. The department has a yearly turnover of around SEK 550 million, out of which about two thirds derive from external funding. IGP has approximately 400 employees, out of which 100 are PhD-students, and there are in total more than 850 affiliated staff members. More information about the department's activities can be found here: www.uu.se/en/staff/department/immunology-genetics-and-pathology Duties Join us at the forefront of pediatric brain tumor research! A Research Assistant position is available in the research group of Veronica Rendo at the Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology at Uppsala University. We are seeking a highly motivated and curious researcher who wants to contribute to cutting-edge research on atypical teratoid rhabdoid tumors (ATRT), a rare and highly aggressive pediatric brain tumor that primarily affects infants and is associated with relapse rates approaching 75%. Our goal is to understand why some tumors respond to treatment while others resist it, and to uncover new therapeutic vulnerabilities that could ultimately improve outcomes for children with ATRT. As part of an interdisciplinary research team, you will investigate mechanisms of treatment response and resistance to standard-of-care therapies as well as clinically relevant targeted treatments. The project is supported by leading Swedish research foundations, including Barncancerfonden, the Göran Gustafsson Foundation, and the Beijer Lab for Gene and Neuroscience, providing a strong environment for ambitious, discovery-driven research. Read more about the project and research group at rendolab.org . As a Research Assistant, you will work with patient-derived brain tumor models and brain organoid co-cultures to investigate tumor biology and treatment response in physiologically relevant experimental systems. The project combines advanced experimental approaches from cancer biology, genomics, and functional genetics, including: - Cell culture of patient-derived brain tumor models - Co-culture of tumor cells with brain organoids - Molecular barcoding and preparation of single-cell RNA-sequencing libraries - CRISPR-Cas12a screening and functional genetic approaches - Viral transduction and BSL-2 work - Flow cytometry and immunofluorescence - Drug response and growth assays - Immunoblotting and other molecular and phenotypic assays You will have the opportunity to work at the intersection of pediatric cancer biology, functional genomics, and emerging model systems, while contributing to research with clear translational relevance. Qualifications We are looking for an enthusiastic and scientifically curious candidate with a Master's degree in biomedicine, medicine, or an equivalent field. Previous hands-on experience with cell culture, including BSL-2 viral work, and molecular biology techniques is expected. Fluency in written and spoken English is required. Above all, we are looking for someone who is eager to learn, enjoys experimental problem-solving, and wants to contribute to a collaborative research environment tackling challenging questions in pediatric cancer. Desirable/Additional Merits Experience in one or more of the following areas is considered a strong advantage: - BSL-2 viral work - Flow cytometry and/or sorting - Molecular cloning - CRISPR-based screening or genome engineering - Epigenetics - Brain tumor biology - Functional genomics or single-cell approaches This is an exciting opportunity to become part of a dynamic research environment and contribute to advancing our understanding of one of the most challenging pediatric brain tumors. If you are motivated by ambitious biological research questions and are eager to develop your experimental skills by working with modern research methods, we look forward to hearing from you. About the employment The employment is a temporary position, 12 months. Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Veronica Rendo, veronica.rendo@igp.uu.se Please submit your application by 16 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2499 Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Special fixed-term employment Pay: Individual salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2499 Last application date: 16 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=965401": {
      "title": "Postdoc position in AI-guided mechanistic understanding of coupled redox–dissolution pathways in multi-metal systems",
      "description": "Postdoc position in AI-guided mechanistic understanding of coupled redox–dissolution pathways in multi-metal systems - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoc position in AI-guided mechanistic understanding of coupled redox–dissolution pathways in multi-metal systems 2026-09-02 The Department of Chemistry - Ångström conducts research and education in the chemistry field. The department has more than 270 employees and has a turnover of 300 million SEK. At the department's six programs, we conduct very successful research of a high international standard. We have a large number of externally funded research projects, often with international cooperation and we see continued good growth in our subject area. The department has education assignments in engineering programs and master's programs. More information is available on our website . (https://kemi.uu.se/angstrom/?languageId=1). Work duties The project focuses on developing a mechanistic understanding of coupled redox–dissolution pathways in multi-metal oxide systems and how these pathways can be inferred from real-time process signals. Using battery-related hydrometallurgical leaching as a model system, the project combines controlled experiments, real-time monitoring, chemical analysis, and data-driven modelling. The postdoctoral researcher will investigate how pH, reduction potential, temperature, hydrogen peroxide consumption, and other process signals reflect competing reaction pathways and evolving kinetic regimes. The work will combine experimental studies, mechanistic modelling, time-resolved data analysis, and machine learning to develop and validate predictive models linking process signals to reaction behaviour, progressing from controlled systems to industrially relevant black masses from battery recycling. The project involves collaboration with two industrial partners and includes a research stay of up to three months at a collaborating university in Finland. The main duties involved in a post-doctoral position is to conduct research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. The duties may also include (e.g.): Research within hydrometallurgy, redox–dissolution chemistry, battery recycling, and data-driven modelling Develop and apply mechanistic and data-driven models to identify reaction regimes and predict dissolution behaviour Analyse time-resolved experimental data using statistical and machine-learning approaches, and validate predictive models using independent experiments Design and conduct controlled leaching experiments in multi-metal oxide systems Perform and analyse time-resolved measurements of pH, reduction potential temperature, hydrogen peroxide consumption, and metal dissolution Investigate reaction kinetics, competing reaction pathways, and evolving surface properties using complementary analytical techniques Disseminate results through scientific publications and presentations at international conferences Collaborate with academic and industrial partners within the project Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies Administration related to the work duties listed above Participation in a research stay of up to three months at a collaborating university in Finland Requirements : PhD degree in Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, Materials Science, Metallurgical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Process Engineering, Data Science or a related field or a foreign degree equivalent to a PhD degree in Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, Materials Science, Metallurgical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Process Engineering, Data Science or a related field . The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Those who have obtained a PhD degree three years prior to the application deadline are primarily considered for the employment. The starting point of the three-year frame period is the application deadline. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. The assessment of applications is based primarily on the applicant's ability to conduct independent research based on scientific skill. Greater importance is attached to the quality of individual scientific work, than to the amount of publications. Consideration will also be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant’s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. The ability to work both independently and collaboratively is of great importance. The application must include a CV, copies of degree certificates and grades. Applications will be assessed according to the following criteria: fulfilment of eligibility requirements, experience in related fields and personal suitability. The working group is small but highly productive with high demands on collaboration skills. The candidate must have very good oral and written proficiency in English. Desirable qualifications Advanced knowledge and/or practical experience in one of the following areas will be beneficial. Experience with machine learning or data-driven modelling, particularly for chemical or process systems Experience with Python, or similar tools for data analysis and modelling Experience with mechanistic or kinetic modelling of chemical processes Experience with hydrometallurgical leaching, redox chemistry, electrochemistry, or reaction kinetics Experience with real-time process monitoring and time-resolved experimental data Experience with multi-component chemical systems, battery materials, or related experimental systems Experience with analytical techniques such as ICP-OES/ICP-MS, XRD, SEM-EDS, or related methods About the employment The employment is a temporary position of 2 years according to central collective agreement, with possibility of extension for one more year depending on the availability of funds. Scope of employment 100%. Starting date 2026-11-01 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Nathalia Vieceli, nathalia.vieceli@kemi.uu.se, phone: +46 70 425 08 89 or Peter Broqvist, peter.broqvist@kemi.uu.se, phone: +46 18 4716274 Please submit your application by 16 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2611 Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Ångström Laboratory Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2611 Last application date: 16 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=961891": {
      "title": "PhD student focusing on Scalable Quantum Program Verification",
      "description": "PhD student focusing on Scalable Quantum Program Verification - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies PhD student focusing on Scalable Quantum Program Verification Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student focusing on Scalable Quantum Program Verification 2026-08-21 Are you interested in working in formal verification and programming language techniques applied to quantum systems, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in a sustainable working environment and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a PhD position at the Department of Information Technology, Uppsala University. The Department of Information Technology holds a leading position in both research and education at all levels. We are currently Uppsala University's third largest department, with 350 employees, including 120 teachers and 120 PhD students. Approximately 5,000 undergraduate students take one or more courses at the department each year. You can find more information about us on the Department of Information Technology website . The position is hosted in a research environment which includes verification experts (Parosh Abdulla, Mohammed Faouzi Atig, Bengt Jonsson, Philipp Ruemmer, Kostis Sagonas, Wang Yi), as well as experts in programming languages (Johannes Borgström, Eva Darulova, Lars-Henrik Erikson, Sofia Ouhbi, Tjark Weber, Tobias Wrigstad). The department is known for both strong theoretical work as well as tool development in these areas (UPPAAL, Concuerror, Nidhugg and other tools), publishing in top conferences such as POPL, PLDI, ICALP and CAV. Project description As both private and public investment in quantum computing continues to surge, the steady upscaling of quantum hardware (now reaching thousands of qubits) has resulted in increasingly sophisticated quantum software pipelines. Given the strategic use of quantum software (e.g. in security), there is an urgent need for verifying the trustworthiness of quantum programs at scale. Features of modern quantum programs such as Quantum Error Correction lead to hybrid quantum-classical architectures, resulting in new challenges for verification. Current tools and techniques do not offer the desired combination of scalability, automation and guarantees to verify such programs. The project aims to address this gap by combining techniques from classical verification and programming language theory with those for complex arithmetic, in order to contribute both theoretical insights and software artifacts advancing the state of the art in quantum program verification. Duties The doctoral student will primarily devote their time to doctoral education. Other departmental duties of at most 20%, including teaching and administration, may also be included in the employment. Requirements To meet the general entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must: hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in computer science or mathematics or a related field, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. The University may permit an exemption from the general entry requirements for an individual applicant, if there are special grounds (Chapter 7, § 39 of the Higher Education Ordinance). For special entry requirements, please see the subject’s general study plan . We are looking for candidates with: a mathematical background, excellent problem-solving skills, high motivation and capacity to persistently work on difficult problems, interest in programming, good communication skills with sufficient proficiency in oral and written English, ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Additional qualifications Experience or coursework in one or more of the following areas is considered an advantage: formal methods, programming language theory or semantics, logic, automata theory, automated theorem proving, and quantum computing. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines . Application The application must include: A statement (max 2 pages) describing the applicant’s motivation, research interests, a concise summary of their Master’s thesis (or comparable project), and the earliest possible starting date; contact information for at least one reference (no reference letter required at this stage). A CV. Degrees and transcripts with grades (officially translated to English or Swedish). The Master’s thesis (or draft), publications, and other relevant self-produced reports. Promising applicants will be invited for interviews before a hiring decision is made. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7. Scope of employment: 100%. Starting date 15 January 2027 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Assistant Professor Ramanathan Thinniyam Srinivasan, email: ramanathan.s.thinniyam@it.uu.se Please submit your application by 15 November 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2571. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what its like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Information Technology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Fixed salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2571 Last application date: 15 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    }
  },
